ne:</b> Consecrated Salt; Incense<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Banshee Wail*, Firestarter, Left-Hand Spanner, Telekinesis<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Ancient Horror</b></span><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 4<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 12, Finesse 9, Resistance 9, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 18<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 9<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 19<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 15<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Anchor 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Unique to each Entity<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Consecrated Salt; Incense<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Fetter, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Banshee Wail*, Drain, Firestarter, Left-Hand Spanner, Regenerate, Speed, Telekinesis</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T17:59:43-07:00","id":993202,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Spirits [Rank 2 &amp; 3] </b></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Asphalt Serpent</b></span><br /> The spirit called \u201cAsphalt Serpent\u201d is a road spirit, who maintains and protects a stretch of winding road approximately 2 miles long. It plagues those who do not pay the proper respect with mechanical failure and other mishaps. The spirit appears as a large black serpentine creature with asphalt for scales and is patterned with road markings. Its eyes flash green, yellow and red.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 4, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Roads 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest on a Roadway; <b>Bane: </b>Soil from beneath a paved crossroad<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Innocuous, Left-Handed Spanner, Pathfinder, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bright Cursor</b></span><br /> Bright Cursor is a helpful (if somewhat alien) spirit that draws essence from computerized devices, such as smart phones or laptops. Bright Cursor appears to be a blinking ball of light surrounded by a cloud of phantom text, images and sounds. It uses its influence to ensure optimum performance<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 6, Resistance 3, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 5, <b>Size</b> 2, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 5, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Communication Devices 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Goes into hibernation if covered in crushed glass; <b>Bane<i>:</i> </b>Fulgurite/Petrified Lightning<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Blast (Electricity), Host Jump, Left Handed Spanner, Sign</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Chains of Vice</b></span><br /> The Chains of Vice is a spirit of death and addiction. Its draws is power from lives lost to excessive indulgence in vice. The entity can take human form, and appears as a tall man, with pale skin, thinning hair, and dressed in a black suit and pork pie hat. In its true form, The Chains of Vice appears as an inhumanly tall and lanky creature, with chalk white skin and no discernable facial features or gender. Its wrists and ankles are bound by chains of brass.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 7, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Addiction 1, Death 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person that has fasted for 3days; <b>Bane:</b> Ashes of an Addict<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Implant Mission, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Rapture, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Covetous Stampede</b></span><br /> \u201cCovetous Stampede\u201d is a spirit of greed who gains essence from the desperate need to obtain popular items. The type of item does not matter; it could be a toy, and athletic sneaker, or the latest smartphone model. As long as people are willing to harm themselves or others to gain the item, Covetous Stampede grows strong. Covetous Stampede appears as a muscular, androgynous creature with the hooves of a bull. Its flesh is patterned with icons and logos of the latest fads, with the symbols older fads fading as they fall out of fashion.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Greed 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest near a recent fad item; <b>Bane: </b>The crushed remains of a recent fad item<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Drain, Rapture, Seek, Sign</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Dreaming Kweo</b></span><br /> The Spirit named \u201cDreaming Kweo\u201d protects the dreams of those that dwell within its territories. It hunts any creature that preys upon dreams, and can travel between the Shadow and Dream Space of a sleeper with ease. When manifested, Dreaming Kweo is a sleek, muscular Mexican gray wolf roughly the size of a horse. His fur is dark as the evening sky, traced with patterns similar to the weave of a dreamcatcher and his eyes, teeth, and claws glow with starlight.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 29<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Dreams 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot withdraw from battle until the enemy retreats or is defeated; <b>Bane: </b>Cottonwood<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Dreamwalker*, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Shattering Howl), Essence Thief, Regenerate, Seek, Speed</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Fanatic Paramour </b></span><br /> The entity called \u201cFanatic Paramour\u201d is a spirit of infatuation taken to unhealthy extremes. The spirit uses its influence to fan idle crushes and passing romantic musings into violent obsessions and feeds on the essence of such acts. It appears as an apparition composed primarily of red vapor; with six dark, sinuous arms and a floating white mask with weeping eyes drawn on the surface.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 7, Finesse 4, Resistance 3, Willpower 7 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 11, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Infatuation 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use influence or numina on a person in a happy romantic relationship <b>Bane: </b>ashes from burned love letters<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Rapture, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Forgotten Pain</b></span><br /> Forgotten Pain is a spirit that feeds on the apathy that some caregivers in hospices and nursing homes develop over time. It uses it powers to manifest as a non-descript middle aged woman dressed in the clothing of a nurse or orderly. Its true form is of an androgynous living statue of ivory. It has a crown of obsidian horns, six arms, and dark eyes that weep black tears.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Apathy 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person wearing Witch Hazel flowers; <b>Bane:</b> Witch Hazel<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Drain, Emotional Aura (Apathy), Mortal Mask, Stalwart, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">He Who Walks Behind the Rows</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 6, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 16, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 18<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Plants 2, Faith 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on a person over 19 years old; <b>Bane:</b> Burning the Cornfields<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Awe, Implant Mission, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Last Merciful Breath</b></span><br /> \u201cLast Merciful Breath\u201d is a spirit of death and mercy. It draws its essence from the final moments of a dying person\u2019s life. It is not a cruel spirit, and uses it power to ease the suffering of the dying. It is powerful, and knows many secrets from long years of traveling the depths of the Underworld. The spirit appears as a skeletal woman wearing a dark veil and a laurel of withered flowers.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 9, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Death 2, Mercy 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest near a dying person; <b>Bane: </b>the ashes of a person tortured to death<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Realm Gateway (Underworld)*, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Essence Thief, Omen Trance, Seek, Speed</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Merchant of Lost Dreams</b></span><br /> \u201cThe Merchant of Lost Dreams\u201d is a spirit of the Pawn Shop, and draws its essence when a person trades a long term desire or precious memento for an immediate need. It has gained great insight into human nature and does not hesitate to use that knowledge for its own gain. The spirit is a dark, slim creature with six long, spindly arms, vaguely human features, and a wide, ever- present grin filled with yellow teeth.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Desire 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can never go back on a Deal; <b>Bane: </b>Pyrite/Fool\u2019s Gold<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Drain, Mixed Blessing (Resources 2)*, Telekinesis, Transmute*</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Molten Stone Fire</b></span><br /> \u201cMolten Stone Fire\u201d is a nature spirit of lava, and dwells in places where volcanic activity impacts human settlement. The sprit is confident, and determined, and takes great delight in burning obstacles into ash. It appears as a child with skin made of cracked black stone with radiant fire appearing within the cracks. Its hair is a wild halo of flames.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Lava 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b> Cannot manifest more than a day\u2019s walk from an active lava flow <b>Bane: </b>Sea Water<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Bane Sense*, Blast (Lava), Firestarter, Pathfinder, Regenerate</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The One Who Burns</b></span><br /> The One Who Burns is a spirit of fire and reckless aggression. It uses it influence to trigger arson and violent outburst s; feeding from the resulting chaos and destruction. The One who Burns takes the form of a vaguely female creature of impressive stature. Its body is cracked and blackened as if by flame and noxious smoke rises from its form. Boiling hot blood seeps from its blistered flesh.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 7, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 13, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fire 2, Violence 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot harm a true pacifist; <b>Bane:</b> Holly (a plant representing peaceful accord)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Posses, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Aggressive Meme, Blast (Fire), Emotional Aura (Anger), Firestarter, Regenerate, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>One Thousand Treacherous Tongues</b></span><br /> \u201cOne Thousand Treacherous Tongues\u201d is a spirit of malicious lies and slander. It gains its essence from those who lie to cause another pain or discomfort, and uses its power to encourage such behavior. It appears as a vaguely female form, with a face, chest, abdomen, and genitals on both the front and back of its body and double-jointed limbs. In both its mouths are multiple lolling tongues, each one over a foot long and jet black. Despite this, the entity speaks clearly and eloquently.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 9, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Lies 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can never utter a truth, will discorporate if forced <b>Bane: </b>White Chrysanthemum<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Dement, Hallucination, Seek, Sign, Spee</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Prince of Hungers</b></span><br /> The Prince of Hungers is a spirit of gluttony and conspicuous consumption. It is often summoned by individuals seeking material gain, especially when the resources are used to support other appetites. When manifested, The Prince of Hungers is a corpulent 10ft tall giant, whose bald head is absent any features except for its oversized mouth with an impossible number of teeth. It always appears in clothing that would consider \u201cfinery\u201d, which could be anything from an expensive suit to opulent robes, all cut to flatter his girth.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Gluttony 2, Wealth 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must consume any edible item presented on a golden platter <b>Bane: </b>Azalea Blossoms<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Drain, Rapture, Stalwart, Telekinesis, Transmute</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Ragged Tear</b></span><br /> The Ragged Tear is a pain spirt that feeds on deliberate cruelty, and uses its influence to compel individuals to greater acts of emotional and physical sadism. It manifests as a dark-skinned, hairless and androgynous person, with empty eye sockets that leak a black fluid and is dressed in tattered wrappings of dark fabric.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Cruelty 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Is repelled by the \u201cAko Konan\u201d, a symbol of West African origin, associated with mercy <b>Bane: </b>Frankincense Resin<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement, Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Scrapyard Mongrel</b></span><br /> Scrapyard Mongrel is a spirit that resides in the scrap yard, it domain the twisting mazes of ruined vehicles and rusted metal. It is a territorial creature, and will attack anyone that enters its territory without the proper appeasement. The spirit is a large canid- seeming amalgam of auto parts and rusted steel, all wrapped in barbed wire and dripping dark oil. Its eyes glow as bright as headlights.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 3, Resistance 5, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 18<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Metal 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest outside of the scrapyard <b>Bane: </b>wood wrapped in leather<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (metal shards), Left \u2013 Handed Spanner, Phantom Arsenal*, Speed, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Shelter of Leaves</b></span><br /> \u201cShelter of Leaves\u201d dwells within a large oak tree that sits in a glade far from the beaten path in a national forest. It has been visited by campers and hikers willing to make the trip for decades. It is a spirit of protection, shielding those within its glade from sun and storm. Shelter of Leaves manifests as a spry old man made of rugged wood, with a beard of leaves and wearing a crown of twigs and acorns.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 4, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 25, <b>Size</b> 16, <b>Initiative</b> 13, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 12<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Trees 2, Protection 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must slumber during Winter <b>Bane: </b>An axe with no wooden elements<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Image, Gauntlet Breach, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Heal*, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Regenerate, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Storm of Dread</b></span><br /> The Spirit called Storm of Dread regains essence when creatures die from electrocution. It formed most of its identity from the execution of death row inmates via the electric chair. Since this form of execution is no longer common, Storm of Dread must seek its essence in other ways. Storm of Dread takes the form of a cloud of black smoke, crackling with lighting and carrying the lingering smells of ozone and burning flesh.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 7, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Electricity 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Loses Essence if submerged in salt water; <b>Bane:</b> Wood struck by lightning<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Claim, Fetter, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Blast (Lightning), Host Jump, Left-Handed Spanner, Regenerate, Speed, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tarnished Badge</b></span><br /> \u201cTarnished Badge\u201d is a spirit that draws its strength from the abuse of the authority granted to police officers and others who enforce the law. The uses its power to urge law officers down the path of corruption. Tarnished Badge appears as a broad shouldered man wearing an antiquated policeman\u2019s uniform. Its face is smooth and featureless except for its eyes, which flash with alternating blue and red light.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 17<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Authority 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot physically harm a law officer unless attacked first; <b>Bane:</b> bones of a person unjustly slain by police<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Revolver), Host Jump, Regenerate, Seek</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Unyielding Lord</b></span><br /> The Unyielding Lord is a spirit of Vengeance, especially acts of vengeance taken to satisfy ones pride. It uses it power to inflame petty insults and minor grievances to a violent extreme. It uses possession frequently, and prefers to occupy the bodies of wealthy professionals. The Unyielding Lord appears as a powerfully muscled red-skinned man, with two heads (each a fierce lion), the wings of an eagle, and writhing swarms of scarabs for arms.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 7, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Vengeance 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Must always keep its Word; <b>Bane:</b> Lily of the Valley (a flower representing humility)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Claim, Fetter, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Implant Mission, Pierce Mind, Regenerate, Seek, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Whisper in the Hall</b></span><br /> Whisper in the Hall is a spirit dwells within schools, and derives its essence from the dedication and pride the students and faculty have for that institution. While normally harmless, it has begun to use its influence to encourage ever greater demonstrations of loyalty and to punish those who do not show the proper amount of \u201cschool spirit\u201d. It appears as a vaguely humanoid swirl of posters, banners and bulletins from the school. It often manifests as a quiet, non-descript student, dressed in the school colors.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Pride 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only influence Faculty, Students or Alumni;<b> Bane: </b>A class ring from a rival school<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Rapture</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 01-15-2017, 11:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:11:26-07:00","id":993204,"title":"","content":"I'm a big Werewolf fan and have always found your spirits to be really useful, even if just a springboard to work off of.<br /> <br /> An upcoming game is going to be somewhat ghost-heavy and was wondering if you had other threads about them, or more than your General Ghosts above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:17:38-07:00","id":993208,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Spirits [Rank 4 &amp; 5] </b></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Crashing Hand of the Tide </b></span><br /> Crashing Hand of the Tide is a spirit of the pounding surf, and is ancient, powerful, and inscrutable. It is endlessly persistent, and once it has decided on a course of action it cannot stop until the task is done. It manifests has a massive luminescent wave of water, shapes can be observed moving within its rippling depths.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 5[Spirit]<br /> Power 13, Finesse 10, Resistance 15, Willpower 10, Essence 50<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 35, <b>Size</b> 20, <b>Initiative</b> 25, <b>Defense</b> 15, <b>Speed</b> 38<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Waves 5, Persistence 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Once it starts a task, it cannot stop until the task is completed; <b>Bane:</b> granite - heated to a burning temperature<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Wave of Water), Drain, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Mother Chrysalis</b></span><br /> The Mother Chrysalis an ancient spirit of metamorphosis that uses its power to physically and spiritually transform those who make the proper offerings and sacrifices to her. The entity appears as a massive black moth with glowing eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 10, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 30<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Metamorphosis 4<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use influence on an unwilling subject; <b>Bane:</b> Powdered moth chrysalis<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Fetter, Image, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Drain, Essence Thief, Heal*, Metamorphosis*, Omen Trance, Regenerate, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Promise of Dust</b></span><br /> The Promise of Dust is a spirit of Drought, and it gains its essence when the land is parched from long periods of little or no rainfall. It uses its power and influence to extend the drought, causing water supplies to evaporate and chasing away rainclouds. When manifested. Promise of Dust is a tall figure with grey, desiccated flesh, wearing a rough spun robe and coated in a fine layer of powdered earth. A stifling heat radiates from its form.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 12, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 18, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 12, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Drought 4, Heat 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest where has not rained in over 30 days; <b>Bane: </b>Natural Rain<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (Desiccation), Drain, Firestarter, Seek, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Screaming Void</b></span><br /> The Screaming Void is a strange spirit from the darker reaches of the Shadow, drawing its power from entropy and dissolution. It appears as a rippling distortion in the air accompanied by a high-pitched resonant noise.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 3, <b>Initiative</b> 18, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 30<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Entropy 3, Sound 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only manifest in locations with a great amount of decay and neglect; <b>Bane:</b> A weapon plated in platinum<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Dement, Entropic Decay, Essence Thief, Left-Handed Spanner, Seek, Speed, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Uktena of the Waterway</b></span><br /> Uktena of the Waterway is a wise old spirit, and has seen many things in its long existence. It has always been willing to use its power and influence on behalf of those who make the appropriate offerings and sacrifices. But something has changed- the spirit has grown violent and capricious, and rumors of it preying upon the local mortals have begun to circulate. Uktena of the Waterway takes the form of an enormous serpent, with scales that shine like crystal and head crowned with the horns of a stag. A large gemstone is affixed in its brow, which glows with a blinding light.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Rivers 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot harm a person that anoints its brow with the blood of a fresh kill; <b>Bane:</b> an arrow wrapped in snakeskin, driven through its heart<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Shadow Gateway, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Blast (Poison Breath), Implant Mission, Innocuous, Omen Trance, Pathfinder, Regenerate, Strike Blind, Twilight Abduction</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-25T18:54:47-07:00","id":993233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993204#post993204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a big Werewolf fan and have always found your spirits to be really useful, even if just a springboard to work off of.<br /> <br /> An upcoming game is going to be somewhat ghost-heavy and was wondering if you had other threads about them, or more than your General Ghosts above?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I have used ghosts, I normally have them linked to haunted/cursed relics. I will post a few such ghosts below. <hr /><b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Ghosts</span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Cassandra Silver</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Cassandra Silver (given name Anne Griswold) was a talented up and coming actress cast the femme fatale in a noir detective film titled Midnight Heart in 1946. During the final week of filming, Cassandra was found dead in her Malibu home. Despite evidence of violence and sexual assault, the city coroner ruled her death \u201csuicide\u201d and the case closed with little fanfare.<br /> Midnight Heart was never released, despite the director\u2019s efforts to edit the film to account for the un-shot scenes.<br /> During the filming the production of an earlier film, Cassandra began an affair with the director which continued on into the production of Midnight Heart. All of this was kept hidden by the studio, as the director was a married man and the scandal would have been disastrous. When she broke off the affair the director flew into a rage and murdered her. The situation was quickly covered up by Solomon Studios and a heavily bribed police force. As most of the people involved are long dead, it is unlikely the truth about Cassandra Silvers death will ever be known.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Her ghost remains anchored to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes?p=806831#post806831\">last known copy of the film</a>.<br /> Cassandra is still a stunning beauty, with blue eyes, porcelain skin, an hourglass figure and silver-blond hair. Although those she sought her revenge against are all dead, Cassandra lingers on.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> <b>Power</b> 5 <b>Finesse</b> 5, <b>Resistance</b> 4, <b>Willpower</b> 9, <b>Essence</b> 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Ambitious, <b>Vice</b> Bitter<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Recapture her fame<br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Expression, Socialize<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Striking Looks 2<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Midnight Heart) 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest where a non-digital filming device is running <b>Bane:</b> Silver<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Telekinetic Thrust), Hallucination, Rapture, Sign, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Sexton Darwin</span></b><br /> Sexton Darwin was the lead vocalist of a 5 member black metal band named \u201cWound\u201d, and was known for a hard-partying lifestyle and dabbling in the occult. The entire band was found dead in late 1990 in what appeared to be a ritualistic murder/suicide. His ghost remains anchored to a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes?p=806817#post806817\">unlabeled black cassette</a> that contains the only known copy of Wound's final album.<br /> Sexton still looks the part of a late 80\u2019s rocker in the black metal scene; black leather pants, black t-shirt, long dark hair and arms covered in satanic and occult tattoos and fists adorned with menacing silver jewelry. Death has made his pale flesh almost white and turned his eyes into smoldering red pinpoints.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> <b>Power</b> 6 <b>Finesse</b> 4, <b>Resistance</b> 4, <b>Willpower</b> 8, <b>Essence</b> 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Artistic, <b>Vice</b> Hatred<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Promote Nihilism and Self Destructive behavior<br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Expression, Occult<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Inspiring<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Black Cassette) 2, Nihilism 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot harm a person wearing a \u201cWound\u201d t-shirt or patch. <b>Bane:</b> Consecrated Salt<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Death Metal Scream), Dement, Implant Mission, Sign</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  updated to Geist 2nd Edition Rules 01-20-2019, 08:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T00:22:27-07:00","id":993363,"title":"","content":"Dude fantastic work as always. <br /> <br /> Have you considered trying to work for onyxpath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T01:23:24-07:00","id":993377,"title":"","content":"Had some prepared Goetia before maybe? Would used some in <b>Mage</b> games I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:14:41-07:00","id":993557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=993363#post993363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude fantastic work as always.<br /> <br /> Have you considered trying to work for onyxpath?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seriously, a folio of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar775_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"775\" data-vbnamecard=\"775\">Reighnhell</a>'s creations would be well worth the price.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-26T10:40:44-07:00","id":993573,"title":"","content":"I'm completely in agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T13:33:32-07:00","id":994786,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the high praise - I am a pretty decent amateur game designer, but I don't think I'm ready for the big leagues yet. Maybe one day.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Goetia</b><br /> I haven't had the chance to run Mage yet, so I haven't come up with any good Goetia just yet. That being said I will see what I can come up with.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, have a new Spirit. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Samhain</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirit known as Samhain is an ancient harvest spirit born from the essence generated by pagan revelers during the festival of Samhain. Over the centuries it has grown and absorbed elements of related traditions (such as Halloween or Dia De Los Muertos), but remains true to its roots. He is an enforcer of custom and ritual, rewarding those who show proper respect to spirits and the memory of the dead, and often punishing those who do not. His current guise is a tall, skeletal figure in tattered robes, with an orb of fire for a head and carrying a lantern made from a turnip with a grotesque face carved into it. The will o wisps of light dance around the lantern. He often takes the form of a child in costume, and accompanies other bands of children as they make their rounds during the holiday.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 12, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 16, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 22, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 28<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Souls 4, Traditions 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only manifest during the time of Samhain (from sunset October 31 to sunset November 1); <b>Bane:</b> An iron sickle or scythe used to harvest crops at least once within the last year.<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Avernian Gateway, Materialize, Reaching, Shadow Gateway, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Aggressive Meme, Awe, Firestarter, Ghost Eater, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Seek</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  Updated 10-29-2016, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:11:26-07:00","id":994823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=994786#post994786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the high praise</div> </div> </div> </div>You deserve it, and more.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=994786#post994786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Samhain</b></span><br /> <b>Influence:</b> Souls 3, Traditions 2</div> </div> </div> </div>Awww. No Influence 4 for Souls or Traditions? Can't create them? :-P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T14:14:12-07:00","id":994826,"title":"","content":"I have a ghost with Influence for Reaping, I think Souls makes more sense, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-28T21:40:15-07:00","id":995070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=994823#post994823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Awww. No Influence 4 for Souls or Traditions? Can't create them? :-P</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya know what? I am going to shift out the Telekinesis Numina for an extra dot of Influence. I like the possibilities of what happens to a person granted a soul stained with Samhain's resonance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T06:18:19-07:00","id":995169,"title":"","content":"All this are wonderfull, i will keep this somewhere for use someday <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm wondering after seeing your Samhain spirit, how would you modelised the mexican Santa Muerte ? A spirit of death ? A strange underworld native ghost-like entities ? An angel of the sort ? I'm curious ^^","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3883-arabidopsis","name":"Arabidopsis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-29T07:52:43-07:00","id":995193,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Santa Muerte</b><br /> <br /> For a figure like Santa Muerte (and the same extends to most other deities and figures of worship), usually don't like putting numbers to them. This is both for the mechanical considerations trying to assign power levels to an actual figure of worship, and out of respect to any that follow said figure.<br /> <br /> That being said, an entity that represents an aspect of such a being can be used to great effect. So while it is unlikely that &quot;Santa Muerte&quot; herself would ever appear in game, any of the following possibilities could be used to great effect. It will depend on the game you are running and for what type of characters.<br /> <br /> A Death Spirit that has grown powerful from the essence generated by her veneration would make an interesting foil for a group of players.<br /> <br /> A Goetic Entity representing her worship could also be used in a game where Astral Entities are prevalent.<br /> <br /> An Ancient Ghost can take on her identity - this could even be the Geist bonded to a Sin Eater.<br /> <br /> An Angel sent by the God Machine to encourage the worship of Santa Muerta, to its own inscrutable ends.<br /> <br /> I will post an example below. This is example is set as a spirit,but can be adjusted to other ephemeral types. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Se\u00f1ora de las Sombras</b></span><br /> \u201cSe\u00f1ora de las Sombras\u201d is a spirit born from the fervent prayers to Santa Muerte -Our Lady of the Holy Death. The spirit is old, but was always of limited power, until recent years when the veneration Santa Muerte has become more and more widespread, radically increasing its power. The spirit considers itself an avatar Santa Muerte (she may even be correct in this assumption), acting on her behalf as an agent of vengeance and protection. Se\u00f1ora de las Sombras takes a form often associated with Santa Muerte \u2013 a skeletal figure dressed as a bride and adorned with jewelry of beads, silver and gold. She carries a golden globe in one hand, and a scythe in the other.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 9, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 17, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Death 3, Protection 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can only manifest where the iconography of Santa Muerte is present <b>Bane: </b>Owl feather bound in silver thread<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Omen Trance, Miracle*, Rapture, Seek<br /> <br /> <b>Numina - Miracle: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.147)</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T12:46:09-07:00","id":996763,"title":"","content":"Excellent creations as always!<br /> <br /> I was wondering if you could try to create some generic Angels. Here are some suggestions for functions:<br /> <br /> 1) A guard who patrols Infrastructure hidden behind common locations such as libraries, museums and warehouses<br /> <br /> 2) A low level employee such as an errand boy who makes sure important messages are sent to the right people<br /> <br /> 3) A high Rank overseer-type who controls a pocket dimension facility where many Angels are created/stored and Demons are imprisoned/reprogrammed. A prime location for Angel-Jacking and a high profile target for a Saboteur mission.<br /> <br /> 4) A Terminator style juggernaut meant to take down particularly powerful supernaturals or stubborn mortals by blending into its surroundings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T13:06:50-07:00","id":996774,"title":"","content":"5) A middle-manager/sub-contractor Angel that manipulates/controls others into building up or tearing down its projects.<br /> <br /> 6) A crowd-sourcing Hunter Angel that uses a combination of information leaks, framing, and hate-plagues to get others to eliminate its targets (structure, phenomena, or creature).<br /> <br /> 7) A low-Rank information kiosk-like Angel that's only job is to get the right piece of information into the right hands, as needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:18:05-07:00","id":996942,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Angels</b><br /> <br /> <i>*Cracks knuckles*</i> <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Terminator style juggernaut meant to take down particularly powerful supernaturals or stubborn mortals by blending into its surroundings. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Chromatic</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Angel known as \u201cChromatic\u201d is an entity designed to track down and eliminate troublesome individuals, typically supernatural entities too powerful to be dealt with by more subtle means. It named for its natural form \u2013 which is a rubbery-fleshed thing that vaguely resembles a cephalopod and glows with a pulsing kaleidoscope of bright colors. This form is rarely seen \u2013 it normally uses it abilities to camouflage itself or possess unassuming mortals in order to get close enough to its quarry to strike.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Angel]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 7, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Unorthodox, <b>Vice</b> Opportunistic<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Deception 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must pursue a chosen target until either the target or Chromatic is destroyed or discorporated; <b>Bane: </b>Hand forged iron weapons<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Host Jump, Innocuous, Pathfinder, Phantom Arsenal, Regenerate, Stalwart</span> <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A high Rank overseer-type who controls a pocket dimension facility where many Angels are created/stored and Demons are imprisoned/reprogrammed. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Curator</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cThe Curator\u201d is an Angel that manages multiple installations within a region where angels are kept between missions. The Curators knowledge of local infrastructure is expansive, and it often debriefs the angels in its care for further information (especially concerning potential threats and obstacles). Despite its immense power, the curator rarely acts directly \u2013 it prefers to act through lower ranking angels that it directs with razor sharp precision. The Angel appears as a towering, androgynous figure, with skin the color of brass and eyes that are softly glowing fields of static. It wears clothing that conveys authority (currently a sharply tailored black suit) but is always barefoot.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 5 [Angel]<br /> Power 13, Finesse 15, Resistance 12, Willpower 10 Essence 50<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 27, <b>Defense</b> 13, <b>Speed</b> 35<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Strategic, <b>Vice</b> Manipulative<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Angels 4, Order 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot directly harm an Angel (but may defend itself); <b>Bane: </b>a blade that has discorporated or destroyed an Angel of rank three or higher.<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Blast (Light), Drain, Implant Mission, Omen Trance, Pierce Mind*, Seek<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Pierce Mind: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition, pg. 211</span> <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A low level employee such as an errand boy who makes sure important messages are sent to the right people </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Signal</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Angel called \u201cSignal\u201d was created to keep lines of communication between differing elements of infrastructure are open and clear. It is deployed to act as a counter agent when enemies of the God Machine work to sabotage communications and spread misinformation. If necessary, the angel is more than capable of delivering particularly sensitive information personally. Signal appears as a boy in early adolescence, dressed in white. His shirt has a red glyph marked on it \u2013 the word for \u201cVoice\u201d in Enochian.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Angel]<br /> Power 3, Finesse 6, Resistance 4, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 13<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Determined, <b>Vice</b> Expressive<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Communication 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot Lie (but can refuse to speak if compelled to lie); <b>Bane: </b>A severed tongue<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Implant Mission, Pathfinder, Seek, Sign, Speed</span> <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A guard who patrols Infrastructure hidden behind common locations such as libraries, museums and warehouses </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Watchman</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Watchman is an Angel tasked with watching designated infrastructure where important objects or information are held. It is frequently assigned to libraries, museums, and warehouses. The Angel always appears as a fit but otherwise non-descript man in his early thirties (details such as race change depending on what would blend in easiest). He wears a dark blue security uniform and wears a silver badge. A radiant light shines from his eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Angel]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 5, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Vigilant, <b>Vice</b> Predictable<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Storage Facilities 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot use influence or numina on personal authorized to be at the location; <b>Bane: </b>A key chain with 7 keys attached<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Left Handed Spanner, Mortal Mask, Regenerate, Seek</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 01-15-2017, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T19:53:52-07:00","id":996957,"title":"","content":"I tip my hat off to you, Reighnhell. These are simply awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T20:14:44-07:00","id":996969,"title":"","content":"Agreed, I could use something like the Chromatic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:54:37-07:00","id":997116,"title":"","content":"Hmm. What Incepts might they possess?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:07:54-08:00","id":999181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A crowd-sourcing Hunter Angel that uses a combination of information leaks, framing, and hate-plagues to get others to eliminate its targets (structure, phenomena, or creature). </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Echo Chamber</span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Angel called Echo Chamber that tracks down and destroys those deemed a threat to one of the God Machines plans. It does so by manipulating others into going after its targets, with favorite medium being disaffected souls that frequent online forums and discussions. From there it will inspire its pawn to violent action (using whatever argument and providing whatever evidence is needed to convince them), and then send it against its true target. Echo Chamber has the body of an androgynous human dressed in contemporary clothing, but its head is a flat screen monitor that shows scrolling lines of code. Faint patterns of circuitry and LEDs lay under its skin.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Angel]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 6, Resistance 3, Willpower 9 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 16<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Internet 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest without a source of electricity nearby; <b>Bane: </b>Glass from a broken CRT monitor<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Implant Mission, Left-Hand Spanner, Rapture, Sign</span> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A low-Rank information kiosk-like Angel that's only job is to get the right piece of information into the right hands, as needed. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Page</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Sometimes the God Machine needs very specific individuals to discover specific information. For this, it sends \u201cPages\u201d \u2013 low ranking angels with little memory beyond a specific topic (but the information about that topic, as well as topics that provide context, it knows extensively). They are subtle, often quietly adding investigations or research that are ongoing or have stalled. When manifest, Pages appear as nondescript female humans with a scholarly or academic mode of dress (typically several years out of fashion.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 1[Angel]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 2, Resistance 2, Willpower 4 Essence 10<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 7, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 4, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 11<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Helpful, <b>Vice</b> Pedantic<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Information (Topic) 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Discorporates if proven wrong about its topic; <b>Bane: </b>Lead<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Image, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Innocuous, Sign</span> <hr /><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A middle-manager/sub-contractor Angel that manipulates/controls others into building up or tearing down its projects. </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Tailor</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Tailor is sent to organize the downfall of organizations on behalf of the God Machine. While its targets are typically cults that have outlived its usefulness, it has also been known to target other groups for reasons no one other than the God Machine can discern. It acts indirectly, severing the strings of fate to engineer the proper sequence of accidents, coincidences, and seemingly random occurrences that tear away at an organizations resource, influence and personnel until it can no longer function. The Tailor appears as a middle-aged man dressed in black with a white tie and carrying a set of highly-polished shears.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Angel]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 12, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 14, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 21, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 26<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Professional, <b>Vice</b> Aloof<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Fate 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Is bound by its word; will honor the intent of any pledge it makes; <b>Bane: </b>a blade made from a set of shears, its handle wrapped in gold wire and coated in hemlock.<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Fetter, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (hurl shears), Fate Sense, Innocuous, Miracle*, Omen Trance, Seek, Speed, Telekinesis</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>*Numina - Miracle: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.147)</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T17:21:41-08:00","id":1002711,"title":"","content":"I think we could use more benevolent spirits (as far as our notions of benevolence can be applied to them). Here are some suggestions:<br /> <br /> 1) A kindness spirit that rewards those who help the poor, sick and defenseless<br /> 2) A courage spirit that enhances the capacities of those who are afraid of pursuing their Aspirations or resolving Conditions<br /> 3) A truth spirit that will help you solve mysteries and other investigations, but demands truthfulness from you too<br /> 4) A justice spirit that helps law enforcers catch criminals and the wrongly accused clear their names","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 11-13-2016, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:02:57-08:00","id":1003736,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Benevolent Entities</b><br /> <br /> The nature of spirits makes depicting them as truly &quot;benevolent&quot; difficult. Even spirits of concepts and things humans would consider positive are still alien and overwhelming selfish creatures. That being said, I like positioning these types of spirits as potential allies in a &quot;quid pro quo&quot; sort of way, or at the very least an antagonist with a more interesting angle than this weeks murder/death/mayhem spirits.<br /> <br /> without further ado.. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Calico Curious</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The entity known as \u201cCalico Curious\u201d is a type of spirit referred to as a <i>Magath</i>, a hybrid of clashing resonances. The spirit is both a cat spirit and a spirit of truth, specifically when it comes to unraveling mysteries of all sorts. It follows detectives, investigative journalists, researchers and others that are dedicated to uncovering truths. Calico Curious appears like its namesake \u2013 a large calico cat with fur patterned like puzzle pieces and glowing orange eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 6, <b>Size</b> 3, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Truth 2, Cats 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot let a lie spoken in its presence go unchallenged; <b>Bane:</b> bones of a domestic cat<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Beast Eyes (Cats), Innocuous, Pathfinder, Speed</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Kindly Stranger</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Kindly Stranger is a wandering spirit that draws essence from acts of charity, particularly from the small acts of kindness bestowed to the poor, the ill, and the oppressed. It often takes human form, walking among the masses offering using its powers to give and relief when necessary. It can occasionally be roused to violence by acts of cruelty or selfishness. It manifests as handsome, older man dressed in black, but its true form is a thick cloud of incandescent gold vapor.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Charity 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot refuse a sincere plea for aid or mercy; <b>Bane:</b> Striga (a type of parasitic plant)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Reaching, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Heal, Know Soul*, Mortal Mask, Rapture, Sign<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Know Soul: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.146)</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Righteous Verdict</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirit Righteous Verdict is an entity of balance and justice that draws it essence when miscarriages of justice are corrected. This does not need to be a legal correction; a falsely imprisoned person escaping satisfies the entity as much as if they are legally exonerated and released. The entity is driven by justice, not law. Righteous Verdict appears in dark robes and a deep hood that obscures it features, it carries a clay tablet in one hand and a worn gavel in the other. Its eyes glow and it speaks in an authoritative but gravelly voice.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 6, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 6, <b>Initiative</b> 15, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Justice 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot use influence or numina on a person rightly exonerated of an accusation or crime within the last year;<b> Bane: </b> remains of a person executed for a crime they did not commit<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Gauntlet Breach, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Pathfinder, Pierce Mind*, Regenerate, Telekinesis, Speed, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Pierce Mind: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (WtF2, pg.211)</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Tomorrow</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cTomorrow\u201d is a spirit of Motivation. It uses its Influence to bolster those who have suffered a defeat or setback to keep working and striving. It will typically focus on a single individual at a time, using its power to push that individual forward to difficulty and hardship. While largely a \u201cpositive\u201d spirit, it does not understand the concept of \u201ccutting losses\u201d and will keep its thrall working towards goals that are unobtainable. Tomorrow appears as an androgynous child, with golden skin and radiant light coming from its eyes and mouth.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 4, Resistance 6, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 12<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Courage 2, Motivation 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest or use influence where someone has committed suicide within the last 10 years; <b>Bane:</b> an implement used in a suicide<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Implant Mission, Rapture, Speed</span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T19:35:49-08:00","id":1003750,"title":"","content":"The Righteous Verdict made me think of <a href=\"http://dcau.wikia.com/wiki/Judgment_Day\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://mutantreviewers.files.wordpress.com/2015/01/04-1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T01:10:52-08:00","id":1003814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1003736#post1003736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> without further ado.. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Calico Curious</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The entity known as \u201cCalico Curious\u201d is a type of spirit referred to as a <i>Magath</i>, a hybrid of clashing resonances. The spirit is both a cat spirit and a spirit of truth, specifically when it comes to unraveling mysteries of all sorts. It follows detectives, investigative journalists, researchers and others that are dedicated to uncovering truths. Calico Curious appears like its namesake \u2013 a large calico cat with fur patterned like puzzle pieces and glowing orange eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 6, <b>Size</b> 3, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Truth 2, Cats 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot let a lie spoken in its presence go unchallenged; <b>Bane:</b> bones of a domestic cat<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Beast Eyes (Cats), Innocuous, Pathfinder, Speed</span></div> </div> </div> </div>It's influences aren't really that alien from one another for me to personally call it a magath. Everybody knows what cats and curiosity entail. Magath are bizarre things, like say, bees made out of lava.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T04:58:52-08:00","id":1003866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1003814#post1003814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's influences aren't really that alien from one another for me to personally call it a magath. Everybody knows what cats and curiosity entail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which would fit if it was curiosity, but cats don't symbolize the truth.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:46:05-08:00","id":1003905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1003866#post1003866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which would fit if it was curiosity, but cats don't symbolize the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the Truth of Cat, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T06:46:25-08:00","id":1003906,"title":"","content":"Sometimes, the line between what counts as a magath and what doesn't can be a little fuzzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T07:03:26-08:00","id":1003917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1003906#post1003906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometimes, the line between what counts as a magath and what doesn't can be a little fuzzy.</div> </div> </div> </div><sub>Pssst. Are we starting a pun war?</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T16:05:02-08:00","id":1004148,"title":"","content":"So, Calico Curious's ban specifies it cannot let a lie in its presence go unchallenged. Does that require it to refute the lie or simply to point it out by, say, simply saying &quot;Lying&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T16:40:32-08:00","id":1004160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1004148#post1004148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, Calico Curious's ban specifies it cannot let a lie in its presence go unchallenged. Does that require it to refute the lie or simply to point it out by, say, simply saying &quot;Lying&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a rank 2 spirit, I'd go with the later. Other similar spirits might be more forceful or even more taciturn about it. Rolling it's eyes when it hears a false statement, for instance. Have it watch Fox News and see how it's eyes go to the back of it's head. Blind tilt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-16T20:41:04-08:00","id":1004226,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Cats Ban</b><br /> <br /> As per usual in such cases, I would leave it to the Storyteller to make the call about the potential nuances of the Ban. But I would run it like this - it would only be blunt when challenging a lie if it does not know the truth.It would make statements like &quot;that is untrue&quot; or &quot;you are incorrect&quot;. If it knows the truth, it would preface its statements with the classic pedantic &quot;Well, Actually...&quot; before presenting the facts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-17T07:13:13-08:00","id":1004392,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/3Af5hBB.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">I feel like a reference has been missed.</a><br /> <br /> I am genuinely surprised the character <i>wasn't</i> a reference to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T09:11:21-08:00","id":1012033,"title":"","content":"Here are a new set, hope you like em'. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Little Glass Weavers</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Little Glass Weavers are small, common spirits that gather around electronic devices. They are largely unobtrusive, and are mostly concerned with keeping electronics working properly. The spirits take the form of spiders, seemingly sculpted from glass and copper and roughly the size of a house cat.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 1[Spirit]<br /> Power 2, Finesse 4, Resistance 2, Willpower 6, Essence 10<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 4, <b>Size</b> 2, <b>Initiative</b> 6, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 12<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Technology 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on non-electronic devices; <b>Bane:</b> Wood<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Innocuous<b>, </b>Left Handed Spanner, Sign</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Throttlewind</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cThrottlewind\u201d is an air spirit that gathers it essence when a living creature asphyxiates. It lurks around those who suffer from respiratory ailments like asthma or emphysema, but has been known to urge individuals to strangle or smother others (or themselves if no other targets are available). The spirit appears as a sinister looking cloud of dingy yellow vapor.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 4, Willpower 8, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 4, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Air 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use Influence or Numina on creatures that do not breathe air; <b>Bane:</b> A weapon made of Tin (a metal associated with Air)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Fetter, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Host Jump, Regenerate</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Wendigo</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Wendigo is an old spirit, associated with cannibalism, famine, and the icy depths of winter. The entity is an insatiable flesh- eater, claiming its victims so it may better prey upon the living, then abandoning them once they have outlived their usefulness. The Wendigo appears as a towering human corpse; emaciated from hunger and frostbitten. Its lips have been torn off, revealing its long yellow teeth. A dull glow emanates from its eyes and its nails are long and sharp.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 29<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Cold 3, Hunger 4<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only manifest on cold (below freezing) winter nights; <b>Bane:</b> Boiling Fat<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Claim, Fetter, Gauntlet Breach, Posses, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Awe, Blast (Icy Wind), Host Jump, Regenerate, Speed</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T15:48:50-08:00","id":1012222,"title":"","content":"I was wondering how you determine things like the Weapon Bonuses of melee attacks, Armor and Doors for ephemeral beings. I used to represent the first and second with Numina called Ravage and Aegis, but have left that behind. I am not sure if it's more fitting to base Doors on Resistance or Rank.<br /> <br /> I'd like to share <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857191#post857191\"><b>some house rules for Angels</b></a> and a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/849897-angelic-form-abilities?p=857443#post857443\"><b>sniper Angel</b></a>. What do you think?<br /> <br /> On a last note, how would you write up Coyote from Navajo mythology?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T15:19:30-08:00","id":1012807,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Re: Spirit Weapons and Armor</b><br /> I have a couple modified Numina I use for this. Please note that spirits are already frightfully powerful when compared to most denizens of the CofD, so these Numina I mostly often employ to help a rank 1 or 2 spirits punch a little harder and survive a little more without moving them up a full rank.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Armored</span></b><span style=\"font-size:11px\">: A spirit with this Numina is difficult to injure, and are often manifest impressively armored forms. The Spirit spends 1 Essence point to gain Armor equalto its rank untilhe end of scene. This armor does not apply against the Spirits Bane.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare Weaponry: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest claws, fangs, horns, suckers, or other appropriate natural weaponry. The modification acts as a 1L weapon.<br /> <i>(This is adjusted from the power of the same name from Beast the Primordial. Pg.236)</i></span><br /> <br /> <b>Re: Spirit Doors</b><br /> I debated this in my games, but ultimately decided to use Resistance. While trying to negotiate against a entity with a potential to start the interaction at +10 Doors can seem daunting, It stresses that entities as single-minded as spirits would be difficult to sway from their aims, and makes it more important for the players to offer <i>Gathra</i> and to actually negotiate with the entity.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Coyote</b><br /> I would consider Coyote to be in the Rank 6+ range, and would most likely be represented by his spirit brood or by lesser avatars of himself.<br /> <br /> Below is an example. I went with a aspect that is a more benevolent interpretation (this could easily be shifted to reflect some of the more sinister depictions of Coyote)</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Gold Eyes Laughing</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cGold Eyes Laughing\u201d is a powerful trickster spirit, who, if asked, claims to be the mythological Coyote himself. While this is likely a lie, few can deny the staggering might the entity possesses. Gold Eyes Laughing reflects the aspect of the trickster that is an agent of change, upsetting routines and breaking patterns. He is benevolent enough that the outcome of his meddling is usually positive, but even he cannot always predict how things will turn out. He is also renowned for his sense of humor, and is filled with a millennia worth of jokes, riddles, and tall tales. Gold Eyes can take many forms, but prefers that of a common western coyote, and anthropomorphic coyote-man, or a handsome Native American man with a mustache and twinkling gold eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 5[Spirit]<br /> Power 13, Finesse 15, Resistance 12, Willpower 10, Essence 50<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 27, <b>Defense</b> 12, <b>Speed</b> 33<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Deception 4, Humor 4<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Gold Eyes Laughing cannot resist an opportunity for (typically) benign mischief; <b>Bane:</b> A stone headed spear; adorned in buffalo hide and eagle feather and stained with rattle snake venom.<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Image, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Essence Thief, Hallucination, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Perfect Lie*, Regenerate, Speed<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Perfect Lie: </b>When this Numen is used successfully, its victim will believe anything it says, no matter how unlikely, as long as it isn\u2019t utter fantasy or contradicted by anything the target knows to be true. The Numen costs one Essence to activate and is contested by Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If the entity succeeds, the victim believes the lie for the scene.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T18:51:21-08:00","id":1020749,"title":"","content":"How do you handle the Claimed in your games, mechanically speaking? Do they use Rank and Essence, or Potency and Willpower points? Also, do you have any guidelines for designing Bans and Banes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 12-21-2016, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T20:50:20-08:00","id":1022201,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Claimed </b><br /> <br /> With Claimed, I run a fairly straight read of the Claimed Condition (distribute power, finesse and resistance to their respective categories, full access to Influence, etc). For Supernatural Tolerance I use the Rank and for determining Dread Powers I give a number of powers equal to the Rank+1 (if using a system where the powers are ranked by dots,give 1+ (Rank x2)). For using its powers, the Claimed uses Essence (or Willpower it it wishes).<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Bans/Banes</b><br /> <br /> These are probably the hardest part of any spirit. My general rule is the same as the book advises - the more powerful the entity, the more obscure/rarefied/situational the bane or ban. I try to come up with things that speak to the nature of the entity. I like banes that are contrary to the nature of the entity (such as a hatred spirit harmed by symbols of love or a water spirit harmed by fire). For Bans, I use them to define the personality of the entity. I like using the Must/Must Not schema, but I also get alot of use from Bans that restrict where, how, or upon who the entity can use its powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 12-26-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T08:04:20-08:00","id":1025437,"title":"","content":"re-watched the Matrix, figured the Menagerie needed one of these guys. <hr /><b>Agents</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cAgents\u201d are servants of the God Machine charged with tracking down and neutralizing &quot;Rogue Elements&quot; - individuals that threaten the plans of the God Machine. Their methods vary, but they are adept at using methods such as blackmail, kidnapping, intimidation, and murder \u2013 all while posing as government agents (or some other authoritative body). Their native form is that of a humanoid silhouette made up of lines of scrolling code, surround by a corona of neon fire. When appearing mortal, they almost always take the shape of \u201cMen In Black\u201d - nondescript but authoritative looking men in dark suits and darker sunglasses.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Angel]<br /> Power 5, Finesse 4, Resistance 5, Willpower 9 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Conformity, <b>Vice</b> Relentless<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Conformity 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot use Influence or Numina on, or Possess, the strong willed (Willpower 6+) ; <b>Bane: </b>Mercury<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Awe, Hallucination, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Speed</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-13T10:17:35-08:00","id":1031230,"title":"","content":"This Nuwisha approves of your Coyote Spirit. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> All seriousness though, your write-ups are BOSS. You should compile them into a pdf resource, a kind of fan-made blue book. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-14T07:15:52-08:00","id":1031569,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Coyote </b><br /> <br /> Thanks! I read through my copy of <i>Changing Breed:Nuwisha</i> before I started that write up.Good to know I was on-target with that one.<br /> <br /> Here are a pair of new Ghosts. As always, feedback is welcome! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Drowned Woman</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">She remembers drowning. It happened so long ago that she has forgotten her name or exactly how she ended up on that ship. But she remembers the storm; months too early in the season and with rain like blades and waves like the fists of an angry god. She remembers the crack of the vessel being torn in half and the cold of the water filling her lungs. She haunted that stretch of coast for decades \u2013tied to a locket given to her by someone she loved (perhaps a husband or fianc\u00e9). But eventually that was worn away by time and tide as well. In life she was a willful woman, and she has continued on in the underworld, becoming a traveler and guide well versed in the many rivers, lakes, and seas that exist within the underworlds winding caverns.<br /> The Drowned Woman appears as a slender woman with bright red hair that stands out against her deathly pale skin and has eyes the color of seawater. Her age is indeterminate, seeming middle aged or youthful by turns. She is dressed in a simple white gown and is perpetually drenched in water as if she just emerged from the waves. She has a lovely voice and sings sea shanties with gusto and skill.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Geist]<br /> <b>Power</b> 8 <b>Finesse</b> 8, <b>Resistance</b> 6, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 11, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Kind, <b>Vice</b> Headstrong<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To help those that travel by waterway<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Expression<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Deep Waters<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot board a vessel without offering payment to the Captain <b>Bane:</b> Tokens of Romantic Affection<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Banshee Wail*, Emotional Aura (Loss), Pathfinder, Seek, Telekinesis<br /> <b><i>Numina \u2013 Banshee Wail:</i></b> The entity creates an earsplitting scream that deafens anyone nearby. Anyone within 20 yards of the entity must succeed on a Resolve + Stamina roll \u2013 the number of successes gained or suffer the Stunned and Deafened Tilt. The Numen costs one Essence to activate.</span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">The Lost Ronin</span></b><br /> The Lost Ronin lived during the waning days of Tokugawa era Japan, and was a Ronin Samurai known for his love of drinking and gambling, and for his entitled attitude towards the peasantry (or anyone else he considered beneath him). After a particularly ugly incident at a gambling hall, he was ambushed by a group of assailants while too drunk to defend himself, as was murdered. His corpse was buried deep in a field and the murderers never spoke of the incident again. His angry spirit lingers on, enraged that he was slain by peasants while drunk, and denied a death befitting a Samurai. Quenching his thirst in the Rivers of Meido have made the Ronin strong, and he longs for re-entry to the world of the living, for only there can he earn a true, worthy, death.<br /> The Lost Ronin has forgotten many details about his mortal life and his appearance has taken on an indistinct quality \u2013 a straw hat that obscures his face and a tattered dark blue kimono are the most striking elements, all other details are a water-color blur.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Geist]<br /> <b>Power</b> 8 <b>Finesse</b> 8,<b> Resistance</b> 8, <b>Willpower</b> 10, <b>Essence</b> 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Proud, <b>Vice</b> Entitled<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> to be put to rest in a manner befitting a samurai<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Weaponry<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Blood<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot refuse a challenge to a Duel <b>Bane:</b> A katana blade wielded by a Samurai (or member of a similar warrior elite)<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Phantom Arsenal (Sword)*, Regenerate, Seek, Speed, Telekinesis<br /> <i><b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal:</b></i> The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  Updated to Geist 2nd Edition Rules 01-20-2019, 08:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T12:50:42-08:00","id":1032272,"title":"","content":"How about some spirits of urban phenomena? Examples:<br /> <br /> 1) Pollution<br /> 2) Poverty<br /> 3) Crime<br /> 4) Prisons<br /> 5) Means Of Transportation<br /> 6) Artistic movements like Hip Hop<br /> 7) Supermarkets<br /> 8) Malls<br /> 9) Movie theaters<br /> 10) Schools And Universities<br /> 11) Tourism<br /> 12) Mega Corporations<br /> 13) Politics<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-15T16:26:08-08:00","id":1032367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GibberingEloquence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1032272#post1032272\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about some spirits of urban phenomena? Examples:<br /> <br /> ...<br /> 13) Politics</div> </div> </div> </div>14) The dread beast, Bureaucracy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T20:22:27-08:00","id":1035030,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Urban Spirits</b><br /> <br /> Cool Suggestions - here are the first few that come to mind. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Counterfeit Shades</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirits referred to as \u201cCounterfeit Shades\u201d are spirits of deception and criminal fraud. Once they were associated primarily with counterfeited currency, but have adapted to gain Essence from acts of embezzlement, identity theft, and credit card fraud. The spirits appear as humanoid figures, wearing clothing that constantly shifts from one style of dress to another, and features that are an unrecognizable blur.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 3, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 13<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Deception 2, Money 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Loses all Willpower if deceived or tricked by non-ephemeral being; <b>Bane:</b> Salt<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Sign</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Hard Place</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cThe Hard Place\u201d is the Spirit of a Maximum Security Prison. In its long years, it has witnessed almost innumerable acts of cruelty, despair, desperation and violence. It now seeks to punish and torment the incarcerated (and has little problem doing the same to the guards and wardens). When manifested, \u201cThe Hard Place\u201d appears as a massive face comprised of concrete with teeth of iron pushing forth from the nearest wall. The features of the face are coarse and its expression is angry or cruelly amused.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 8, Resistance 12, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 20, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 12, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Prison 4, Punishment 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Loses all Willpower if a Prisoner Escapes; <b>Bane: </b>Ink from a pen used to sign an official Pardon<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Image, Posses, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Emotional Aura, Essence Thief, Implant Mission, Stalwart</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Lean Fortune</b></span><br /> \u201cLean Fortune\u201d are spirits of poverty and the bad luck that often plague those of little means. It uses it influence to cause minor misfortunes and financial setbacks to ensure that the impoverished stay that way. They appear most often as thin, shadowy figures, wearing faded and threadbare cast-off clothing.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 3, Resistance 5, Willpower 8, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 10, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 8, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 12<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Poverty 2, Misfortune 1<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Cannot use influence or numina on those wearing the trappings of luxury; <b>Bane:</b> Gold<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Entropic Decay, Left-Handed Spanner</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Poison Black Fog</b></span><br /> The entities known as \u201cPoison Black Fog\u201d are Spirits of Smog and are common in cities and environments with a high degree of air pollution. They manifest as wispy clouds of dark, polluted vapor and are frequently found in the company of factory or automotive spirits.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 3, Finesse 6, Resistance 3, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 5, <b>Size</b> 2, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Smog 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Becomes weakened in places without readily detectable air pollution; <b>Bane:</b> green wood<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Discorporate, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Drain, Innocuous, Seek</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 01-22-2017, 01:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-20T08:08:59-08:00","id":1035225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1035030#post1035030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Counterfeit Shades</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirits referred to as \u201cCounterfeit Shades\u201d are spirits of deception and criminal fraud. Once they were associated primarily with counterfeited currency, but have adapted to gain Essence from acts of embezzlement, identity theft, and credit card fraud. The spirits appear as humanoid figures, wearing clothing that constantly shifts from one style of dress to another, and features that are an unrecognizable blur.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 3, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 9, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 13<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Deception 2, Money 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Loses all Willpower if deceived or tricked by non-ephemeral being; <b>Bane:</b> Salt<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Implant Mission, Sign</span></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kinda surprised this one doesn't have Mortal Mask (and Materialize). And Discorporate. For the &quot;Pretend to be someone, then Discorporate to get out of dodge when found out&quot;. I could easily see the scummy spirit-bastard selling bad bootlegs, then vanishing once you turn around.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:32:24-08:00","id":1036058,"title":"","content":"<b>Re:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Counterfeit Shades</b><br /> <br /> The picture I had in mind for these spirits was a whispering,insidious influence. But I like your suggestion more, so I am making that update. Thanks!<br /> <br /> <b>Re: More Urban Spirits </b><br /> <br /> Working my way down the list.</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>All Shop</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">An \u201cAll Shop\u201d is a spirit associated with malls, supermarkets, and other shopping centers. As the local shopping center is often a focal point of a neighborhood, an All Shop can grow powerful as they feed on the lesser spirits that congregate near their physical reflections. The often have personalities that reflect their clientele, All Shops from affluent neighborhoods can be elitist and discriminating, while those from poorer places can seem desperate and opportunistic. The spirits typically appear as large, anthropomorphized versions of their physical reflection, but can materialize as non-descript people in the clothing of a store employee (often a manager or cashier).<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 6, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 18, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 6, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Commerce 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Goes into hibernation if the store operates at a loss for more than a month; <b>Bane: </b>Bricks taken from a market that has gone out of business and been demolished<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Reaching, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Sign, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Break Beat</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cBreak Beat\u201d is a spirit of artistic expression, born in the earliest days of hip-hop from the then-revolutionary hip hop DJs and MC\u2019s. As the techniques have grown and evolved and even spread to other genres, so has Break Beat\u2019s power. Despite its increased influence, the spirit retains a rebellious, counter culture nature, and instinctively fights against \u201cThe Establishment\u201d in its myriad forms. The spirit appears a luminescent apparition of a young African American man dressed in contemporary club fashion (but still sports the Kangol hat and heavy gold ropes of earlier hip style).<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 8, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Music 3, Rebellion 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Goes into hibernation if defeated in a DJ or MC Battle; <b>Bane: </b>Magnets from a speaker made prior to 1980<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Blast (Bass), Emotional Aura, Implant Mission, Mortal Mask, Sign</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Engine Twelve</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirit called \u201cEngine Twelve\u201d awoke during a horrific accident, where the subway train that is its physical reflection lost control and slammed into a crowded platform, killing many and maiming others. Since then, the spirit continues to roam the dark reaches of the subways, hunting down and devouring any foolish enough to wander the deeper recesses of the labyrinthine subway network. It takes the appearance of a nightmarishly exaggerated subway train engine, with a grill like crooked teeth and a headlight with a blinding white glare.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Spirit]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 6, Resistance 10, Willpower 10 Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 30, <b>Size</b> 20, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 38<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Accidents 2, Trains 3<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only travel on or near rail lines <b>Bane: </b>glass from the original physical Engine 12<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Gauntlet Breech, Image, Materialize, Shadow Gateway, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Banshee Wail, Phantom Arsenal, Speed, Stalwart, Strike Blind<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Banshee Wail: </b>The entity creates an earsplitting scream that deafens anyone nearby. Anyone within 20 yards of the entity must succeed on a Resolve + Stamina roll \u2013 the number of successes gained or suffer the Stunned and Deafened Tilt. The Numen costs one Essence to activate.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Strike Blind: </b>The entity using this Numen may blind people over an area, whether using darkness or blinding light (chosen when gained and appropriate to the entity in question). Activating the Numen requires 1 Essence and affects an area with a radius of the entity\u2019s Power in yards, causing the Blinded Tilt. Characters may resist with Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance. The effect is magical in origin but can be dealt with in mundane fashion, such as by activating light sources to partially negate darkness or a welder\u2019s mask to help reduce blinding glare. The Tilt lasts until the entity dismisses it, leaves the area, or the scene ends.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Flickering Usher</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">A \u201cFlickering Usher\u201d is a type of spirit that is associated with movie theatres. They are mercurial; shifting through personae\u2019s absorbed from countless of hours of film and the emotional experience of thousands of movie goers. They also know an amazing amount of movie trivia. Most theatres only have a single Flickering Usher (if any), but large or popular venues might support several. They appear as a humanoid form made from flickering light and speak in hushed tones (unless quoting a film, which they do perfectly). They can manifest in human form, typically that of either a theatre employee, or a character from a recent (or particularly popular) film.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 6, Resistance 4, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 20<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Movie Theatre 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Can take no action (other than watch) if a film is running. It can defend itself if attacked; <b>Bane: </b>Shard of glass from a television screen.<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Mortal Mask, Sign</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:25:49-08:00","id":1036153,"title":"","content":"Would a Mall spirit reside over a spirit court of the more popular shops within it and other spirits of greed and commerce?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T22:56:33-08:00","id":1046645,"title":"","content":"Do you think you can create ghosts like the ones I described in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1046190#post1046190\"><b>this post?</b></a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-11T09:16:48-08:00","id":1047258,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Mall Spirit </b><br /> <br /> I would say the spirit court of a Shopping Center/Mall would be circumstantial. The spirit of a thriving shopping plaza might be powerful enough to rule over the spirits of the constituent stores and attendant commerce spirits. A slowing dying mall kept afloat by one or two popular storefronts might actually be subservient to those spirits, if it exists as a unique entity at all.<br /> <br /> <b>Re:Ghost of the City</b><br /> <br /> After reviewing that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/864699-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-general-chronicles-world-of-darkness?p=1047230#post1047230\">thread</a>, I can put together an example Ghost. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Councilman Tracy</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Niles Tracy had always been civic minded. Throughout his youth and well into middle age, Niles had been involved in local politics \u2013 from door to door campaigns, to fund raising, to serving on the city council. He made it his personal duty to fight the corruption in government he saw all around him, and eventually realized that the source of much of this corruption were creature that could only be called Vampires. Luckily, he soon was approached by like-minded individuals who aided him in his fight against the influence of these creatures (which was far deeper and more insidious than he ever suspected). His life ended when he was pulled over while driving him by a police officer; the last thing he saw was the flash of the pistol firing into his face. The crime was attributed to known ex con who enthusiastically confessed to the crime. Since then, the ghost of Councilman Tracy lingers on, haunting City Hall and the surrounding neighborhood. He uses his powers to fetter himself to others he know the truth about the undead and aid them however he can.<br /> Councilman Tracy appears much as he did in life; a middle\u2013aged man with greying hair and a kind face, wearing a dark grey suit with a gold tie. Where his right eyes would be is a ragged gunshot wound.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> Power 4 Finesse 6, Resistance 4, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Civic Minded, <b>Vice</b> Meddlesome<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To curb Vampiric Influence in city affairs</span><br /> <b>Key Skills:</b> Persuasion, Politics<br /> <b>Key Merits:</b> Professional Training (Politician)<br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Influence:</b> Anchor (City Hall) 2<br /> <b>Ban: </b>Can only use Numina and Influence on those who know Vampires exist <b>Bane:</b> Salt<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Fetter, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Implant Mission, Seek, Sign, Telekinesis</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  Updated to Geist 2nd Edition Rules 01-20-2019, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-12T12:49:32-08:00","id":1047825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1036058#post1036058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> An \u201cAll Shop\u201d is a spirit associated with malls, supermarkets, and other shopping centers. As the local shopping center is often a focal point of a neighborhood, an All Shop can grow powerful as they feed on the lesser spirits that congregate near their physical reflections. The often have personalities that reflect their clientele, All Shops from affluent neighborhoods can be elitist and discriminating, while those from poorer places can seem desperate and opportunistic. The spirits typically appear as large, anthropomorphized versions of their physical reflection, but can materialize as non-descript people in the clothing of a store employee (often a manager or cashier).</div> </div> </div> </div>So a question about conceptualizing &quot;building-spirits&quot; like All Shop: do you consider the spirit of say a supermarket to be distinct from the spirit of the supermarket building? For example, let's say there is a spirit of Wal-Mart. Would it be a separate, distinct entity from the spirit of the Wal-Mart building? Or would the spirit of Wal-Mart look and act like the building itself? Or would the spirit reside within a spiritual reflection of the building, sort of like a liar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5700-nuwisha-nutjob","name":"Nuwisha Nutjob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5700_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-15T22:21:07-08:00","id":1049701,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Building Spirits</b><br /> <br /> I most cases, the &quot;Spirit of the Store&quot; and the &quot;Spirit of The Building that Houses the Store&quot; are one and the same. Any distinction between the two is so minor as to not have any practical difference. The spirit could still appear as something that lives within the building rather than the building itself, but its powers an influences would be the same as another spirit of the same type but of a more literal manifestation. Of course, all of this is how I conceptualize and run things in my games (YMMV, as always).<br /> <br /> <b>Re: More Spirits</b><br /> Been a while since I put up some content, so lets continue with a few more Spirits of Urban Phenomena. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Academy Principle</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The spirits called \u201cAcademy Principles\u201d are the awakened spirits of an educational institution. They embody the ideals of the institution and experiences of students, faculty and surrounding community. Because of this, their personalities can vary wildly; one can expect the spirit of a private school for gifted students to be quite different than an inner city public school. But even in light of this variance, Academy Principles are almost always formal, erudite and tradition minded. The Academy Principles appear as tall humanoid figure, dressed in cap and gown (or other ceremonial clothing). Its features are a semi-transparent shadow with brightly glowing eyes and it always carries a heavy tome.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Spirit]<br /> Power 8, Finesse 9, Resistance 8, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 17, <b>Defense</b> 8, <b>Speed</b> 17<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Educational Institution 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest when school is not in session; <b>Bane: </b>ashes of a diploma burned by the graduate<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Image, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Hallucination, Implant Mission, Innocuous, Sign, Telekinesis</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Company Men</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The \u201cCompany Men\u201d are spirits associated with large businesses or corporations. These entities serve as enforcers of the company\u2019s philosophies and practices \u2013 using their influence to promote the culture while quashing dissent. While a given \u201cCompany Man\u201d is of relatively limited power, individual spirits (especially those of powerful and well-known companies\u201d can become incredibly potent. Despite their names, \u201cCompany Men\u201d appear as blandly attractive male or female humans, dressed in a \u201cbusiness casual\u201d style. This is a fa\u00e7ade, as any tear to their flesh or removal of clothing will reveal a completely hollow interior.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Spirit]<br /> Power 4, Finesse 6, Resistance 4, Willpower 10 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 9, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 10, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 15<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Loyalty 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot act outside of Corporate Policy;<b> Bane: </b>A written notice of termination<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Aggressive Meme, Innocuous, Mortal Mask, Rapture</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Travel Guides</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u201cTravel Guides\u201d are strange spirits that use their influence to convince others to travel. They are spawned from wanderlust and attracted to those who desire to travel but never get the opportunity. They are largely harmless, but ones that grow powerful can compel their targets to act upon their desires \u2013regardless of consequence. The spirits appear as small, somewhat animalistic beings, with the long limbs of a natural runner and large inquisitive eyes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 1[Spirit]<br /> Power 3, Finesse 3, Resistance 2, Willpower 5 Essence 10<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 5, <b>Size</b> 3, <b>Initiative</b> 5, <b>Defense</b> 3, <b>Speed</b> 14<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Wanderlust 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot stay fettered to a single person or place for more than three sunrises;<b> Bane: </b>Marble<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Fetter, Unfetter, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Pathfinder, Speed</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:26:02-08:00","id":1050063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1049701#post1049701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Building Spirits</b><br /> <br /> I most cases, the &quot;Spirit of the Store&quot; and the &quot;Spirit of The Building that Houses the Store&quot; are one and the same. Any distinction between the two is so minor as to not have any practical difference. The spirit could still appear as something that lives within the building rather than the building itself, but its powers an influences would be the same as another spirit of the same type but of a more literal manifestation. Of course, all of this is how I conceptualize and run things in my games (YMMV, as always).</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other side of the spectrum, you could consider a Mall spirit as being a host to several other kinds of spirit. Think a living organism, just like it becomes part of a larger system when you consider the city in which it is housed. The minimalist approach works fine to keep things small and personal, but mine's more verisimilar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:25:58-08:00","id":1055530,"title":"","content":"Do the existing rules allow for the epynonomous room of Stephen King's Room 1403 to be written up as a Spirit or Ghost fetters/anchored to a room. Stuff like sending surreal phone messages and disappearing all the adjacent windows when he tries to climb along the ledge into another room to escape seem reasonable. But at one point, he hallucinate leaving the room and a month or so of normal life before the room ends it. I'm not sure if the Hallucination power can do compressed time experiences like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T03:53:17-08:00","id":1055587,"title":"","content":"A fettered entity can't use Numina, and can only use Influences on its fetter. It'd have to be someone with Influence: Creepy \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022, and liberal use of that Influence, but even then I don't think the month long hallucination (or the time reset) is within its scope since whatever power that is would definitely be used on the character and not the room. Influence: Time \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 should be able to create another night, but still doesn't explain the hallucination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:27:34-08:00","id":1055932,"title":"","content":"I don't think a month actually passed. I think it was like a dream, where something that lasts less than a minute in real time can be experienced as an epic movie length adventure in your head","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:28:53-08:00","id":1056938,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: 1403</b><br /> <br /> At least as I would run it, an Ephemeral Anchored/Fettered to a room would be able to use its Numina on those inside of the room as per usual Manifestation rules (the room would have the <i>Open</i> Condition)<br /> <br /> As for the <i>Hallucination</i> Numina, since each success allows the Entity to alter one of the targets senses, I would say that an exceptional success would allow the full sensory hallucination - up to and including distorting the targets sense of time or generating a fabricated reality (although I might limit such degree of power and control to entities of rank 3 or greater).<br /> <br /> <b>Re: More Spirits</b><br /> <br /> here are a few more generic elemental spirits <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Air Spirit </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank:</b> 2 (Spirit)<br /> Power 4, Finesse 7, Resistance 3, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 10<br /> <b>Defense: </b>4<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 21<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Air 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest in an airless environment<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Pulverized Stone<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Electric Jolt), Innocuous, Speed, Telekinesis</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Earth Spirit </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank:</b> 2 (Spirit)<br /> Power 5, Finesse 3, Resistance 6, Willpower 10, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense: </b>6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 13<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 12<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Earth 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must Discorporate if separated from the ground<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Electricity<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Armored*, Blast (Stone Shards), Pathfinder, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Numina - Armored:</i></b> A spirit with this Numina is difficult to injure, and are often manifest impressively armored forms. The Spirit spends 1 Essence point to gain Armor equal to its rank until the end of scene. This armor does not apply against the Spirits Bane.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Fire Spirit</span> </b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank:</b> 2 (Spirit)<br /> Power 5, Finesse 5, Resistance 4, Willpower 9, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 9<br /> <b>Defense: </b>5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 20<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 9<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Fire 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest more than 10 feet away from an open flame<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Ice Water<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Fire), Emotional Aura (Fascination), Firestarter, Speed</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Water Spirit </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank:</b> 2 (Spirit)<br /> Power 6, Finesse 3, Resistance 5, Willpower 8, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 8<br /> <b>Defense: </b>5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 15<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Water 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest more than 10 feet away from open water<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Heated Metal<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Water Torrent), Innocuous, Regenerate, Stalwart</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T21:33:53-08:00","id":1056972,"title":"","content":"... Make a Heart Spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T23:18:51-08:00","id":1057000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1056972#post1056972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Make a Heart Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>And from combination of Spirits come he... CAPTAIN PLANET! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T04:53:52-08:00","id":1057048,"title":"","content":"Re: 1403<br /> <br /> Was imagining it as a pretty high-ranking epheremal anyway, such as a Rank 4+ ghost who had spent centuries in the Underworld before it's summoning or a Torment Spirit that has gorged itself on the Resonance of its own grisly legend","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T04:59:20-08:00","id":1057050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1057000#post1057000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And from combination of Spirits come he... CAPTAIN PLANET! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who would probably be more like the homicidal Ted Turner from Robot Chicken than the TV version.<br /> <br /> Speaking of that, do you think a Spirit of Environmentalism would try to stop pollution? Or would they make sure it stays around in some capacity so they can keep feeding on Resonance from angry activists?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T11:30:05-08:00","id":1057168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1057050#post1057050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Who would probably be more like the homicidal Ted Turner from Robot Chicken than the TV version.<br /> <br /> Speaking of that, do you think a Spirit of Environmentalism would try to stop pollution? Or would they make sure it stays around in some capacity so they can keep feeding on Resonance from angry activists?</div> </div> </div> </div>The later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:09:01-08:00","id":1057309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1057168#post1057168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The later.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's what I was thinking, but it could be that the Spirit is too short-sighted to realize that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:27:42-08:00","id":1057321,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Rank. It may act like an eco-terrorist, destroying anything that has the slightest effect on the environment.<br /> <br /> On one hand, lower Rank spirits are more concerned with the here and now, on the other hand, higher Ranked spirits tend to expand their purview. One might do neither, and instead just linger around humans using Aggressive Meme, since the envorinmentalism concept is a thought more than an action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-02-2017, 07:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T22:47:17-08:00","id":1057472,"title":"","content":"Here's a challenge for you, Reighnhell. Can you create some magath by rolling 2d20 and combining the corrensponding concepts from the list below? Feel free to create as many as you want and to discard combinations you find too implausible or uninteresting.<br /> <br /> 1) Freedom<br /> 2) Change<br /> 3) Beauty<br /> 4) Technology<br /> 5) Responsibility<br /> 6) Ignorance<br /> 7) Nostalgia<br /> 8) Retribution<br /> 9) Hospitality<br /> 10) Wisdom<br /> 11) Art<br /> 12) Corruption<br /> 13) Adventure<br /> 14) Betrayal<br /> 15) Redemption<br /> 16) Rethoric<br /> 17) Secrecy<br /> 18) Nobility<br /> 19) Revulsion<br /> 20) Suffering","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T12:09:27-08:00","id":1057701,"title":"","content":"I have a request as well, if it's not a bother. There's a lot of words and I apologize in advance.<br /> <br /> My group of mages has stumbled onto a pylon of Seers that I've taken from the Sanctum &amp; Sigil book, starting around p137. If you have it, great. If not, here's the gist. Hedonistic Satanic cult leader William Harris was a mage and didn't know it, seeing his powers through his own lens for a while before the Seers actually got to and recruited him. He's more open minded about the Supernal world, but he's reconciled the Exarchs so that they fit into his belief system and has gathered other broken, mostly like-minded Seers to his cult and manor. They're styled after the Four Horsemen, with him being the architect of the Apocalypse, guided by the dreams given to him by the Exarch-Gods. The 'Apocalypse' is smaller scale than the word would suggest and he believes the goal is to wipe the city of all opposing mages. Still an impressive act if he pulls it off. The Horsemen are Death, a six-year old Awakened girl obsessed with, naturally, Death for whom people are as expendable as dolls and who has already killed her parents by animating the family pet they had put down. Pestilence is an introverted and agoraphobic teenage boy, I'd think the pestilence is more of the mind considering his outlook, and he's the Judas in the group, actively plotting betrayal while the others are willing to follow Harris until they see a better option. War is an ex-Adamantine Arrow who was tired of being used by his Order and decided to wage war against them, he's got a penchant for animating suits of armor he's fitted to be especially good as 'grunts' in combat. Famine was a repeated victim of abuse who hungers for dominance and strength and meditates in states of extreme submission. They keep a girl prisoner in the basement, switching her out when the last one dies or gets worn out. They torment the 'guest' with Mind and Life magics, and they use their Profane Urim, an artifact that allows for the entire pylon to use it simultaneously to achieve the psychic domination of people, which they seem to use for practical and 'entertainment' purposes.<br /> <br /> Infodump over.<br /> <br /> It's as ugly a place as its owners, I've styled it visually a bit after the Resident Evil mansion. A place built by extravagant wealth but neglected as the people inside turned to their own devices.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://vignette3.wikia.nocookie.net/residentevil/images/9/93/Spencer_Estate.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> While working with it I noticed none of the mages had any strong spiritual leanings. Two people had Spirit 1, and I decided to put those dots elsewhere so they could remain entirely ignorant of the spiritual landscape, which has since become a Wound. And where there's a Wound, there's a Maeltinet.<br /> <br /> So specifically, I'm looking for a Rank 4 Maeltinet, either pure spirit or immundi, that might fit given the atmosphere, events and occupants of the place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T16:42:39-08:00","id":1058650,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Magath -a - matic</b><br /> <br /> I am looking forward to playing around with this. I haven't really create many Magath, but they are always great to keep the players guessing.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: The Ugly Place</b><br /> <br /> I am giving this alot of thought - I am trying to come up with the proper representation of a spirit that would arise in the shadow of such powerful yet thoroughly toxic people.<br /> I am definitely going with Maeltinet/Immundi, so much so I had to take a stab at revising some the Inferno mechanics for 2nd Edition. Since it might a bit before I can put more energy into this, here are my notes so far. Feedback welcome as always. <hr /><br /> Here are the broad notes. I put down where Infernal Entity (since the word &quot;Demon&quot; is somewhat worn out by now) differs from baseline Ephemeral rules.<br /> <br /> <b>Infernal Entities (Diaboli &amp;Dominions)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Rank: </b>Dominions run the full range of Ranks. Ephemeral Entities that become Diaboli retain their Rank. Corrupted Ghosts become <i>Larvals</i>, Corrupted Goetia become <i>Deceptors</i> and Corrupted Spirits become <i>Immundi</i>.<br /> <b>Native: </b>Dominions are native to a ream called the Inferno (or simply \u201cHell\u201d)<b>. </b>Corrupted Ephemeral entities retain their ties to their original realms (if any).<br /> <b>Virtue/Vice: </b>Diaboli and Dominions don\u2019t have a Virtue or Vice. Instead, they have a <i>Malpraxis</i>; typically consisting of a sinful act and the circumstances of when, where, or how it is indulged. Diaboli and Dominions recover Willpower when someone else indulges in behavior that aligns with their <i>Malpraxis</i>.<br /> <b>Language: </b>Diaboli and Dominions understand all languages, including dead languages or languages used by other supernatural entities. In addition, Diaboli and Dominions speak \u201cDragons Tongue\u201d; a twisted glossolalia that is spoken and understood by the Infernal Entities, but cannot otherwise be translated or deciphered.<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>Diaboli and Dominions don\u2019t have an Integrity trait.<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Diaboli and Dominions have Influences that relate to their Malpraxis, with Diaboli often retain influences they possessed before their corruption.<br /> <b>Essence: </b>Infernal Entities require the <b><i>Corrupt</i></b> Condition in order to regain Essence and prevent Essence Bleed. Depending on the nature of the entity, they may also be able to make use of the <i><b>Anchor</b></i> or <i><b>Resonant</b></i> Condition. Diabolists or Cultists sacrificing precious resources (metaphorical or literal), animals, or even humans to the Infernal Entity in its presence allow it to regain the Resources value of the item or animal, or the current Integrity of a human sacrifice, as Essence.<br /> <b>Secrets &amp; Lies: </b>No supernatural ability can reveal a Diaboli or Dominions lies, half-truths and other deceptions for what they are. Anyone using the power will see the result the Infernal Entity wants them to see. Likewise, no supernatural ability can read the mind or intrude upon the thoughts of an Infernal Entity.<br /> <b>Soul of Sin:</b> Infernal Entities have the <b><i>Know Soul</i></b> Numina (the same as the Dread Power).</span> <hr />Below are some supporting Manifestations, Conditions and Numina.<br /> <br /> <b>Corrupt (Condition)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Description: </b>The subject of this condition is within the sphere of Influence of an Infernal Entity.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>Corruption can be caused by the extended efforts of Diabolists and unwitting pawns, or by the direct involvement of Infernal Entities. It can also occur naturally, typically in places where acts of evil have been committed routinely or where particularly heinous events have transpired. Powerful, high ranking Infernal Entities can use Influence to instill this Condition.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>Destroying the corrupt object or place can End this condition. Prolonged efforts to cleanse the affected place or supernatural abilities to alter resonance can also end the Condition. Finally, abjuration and exorcism may temporarily suppress the Condition.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Whisperer (Condition)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Description: </b>The entity has secured itself to an object or creature. As long as it remains a Whisperer, the entity is safe from Essence Bleed. While this Condition is applied, the entity exists in twilight near the target, but is wholly insubstantial and invisible and cannot interact with other entities in Twilight without the use of additional supernatural powers. The entity gains access to the Adjust Reality and Sign Numina, even if they would normally not have these abilities. Besides these two, the entity cannot use any other Numina or Influence on the target and cannot use any other Manifestation Effects, but may communicate directly with the targets mind and influence the targets dreams.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>This Condition is created by an entity using the Whisperer Manifestation Effect.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The entity can voluntarily end the Condition at any time, but doing so discorporates the entity with all the normal consequences. Whisperers are also easier to banish, and all abjuration and exorcism rolls against it receive a +2 bonus.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Whisperer (Manifestation)</b><br /> This manifestation is common to Infernal Entities. With it they can slowly lure a targeted individual into sin and depravity. This is similar to the Fettered Manifestation, but does not require the Open Condition. By spending 2 Essence, the entity adds the Whisperer Condition to itself. Beings targeted by this Effect contest the roll with Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If the Effect is successful, targets gain the Urged Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Adjust Reality</b><br /> This Numina allows the entity to subtly shift reality. This typically manifests a streak of luck or sudden opportunity, which the entity can exploit to their benefit. Once per scene, when the entity spends Willpower to add to a dice pool it may reroll a number a failed dice up to its rank. If spending Willpower to bolster Defense, it may force the opponent to reroll successful dice equal to its Rank. Alternatively, the entity can grant an individual other than themselves a die bonus of +2 to a single roll, as they adjust reality to accommodate their whims.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T03:13:29-08:00","id":1058855,"title":"","content":"You have no idea how much I'm thanking you for the Inferno rules, even if it's only a little bit of the full content. Now I understand what some posters meant when they were sad for not being able to Like more than once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-06T22:42:51-08:00","id":1059359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1058650#post1058650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Whisperer (Condition)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Description: </b>The entity has secured itself to an object or creature. As long as it remains a Whisperer, the entity is safe from Essence Bleed. While this Condition is applied, the entity exists in twilight near the target, but is wholly insubstantial and invisible and cannot interact with other entities in Twilight without the use of additional supernatural powers. The entity gains access to the Adjust Reality and Sign Numina, even if they would normally not have these abilities. Besides these two, the entity cannot use any other Numina or Influence on the target and cannot use any other Manifestation Effects, but may communicate directly with the targets mind and influence the targets dreams.<br /> <b>Causing the Condition: </b>This Condition is created by an entity using the Whisperer Manifestation Effect.<br /> <b>Ending the Condition: </b>The entity can voluntarily end the Condition at any time, but doing so discorporates the entity with all the normal consequences. Whisperers are also easier to banish, and all abjuration and exorcism rolls against it receive a +2 bonus.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Whisperer (Manifestation)</b><br /> This manifestation is common to Infernal Entities. With it they can slowly lure a targeted individual into sin and depravity. This is similar to the Fettered Manifestation, but does not require the Open Condition. By spending 2 Essence, the entity adds the Whisperer Condition to itself. Beings targeted by this Effect contest the roll with Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance. If the Effect is successful, targets gain the Urged Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm much more like Whispers to be ONLY Condition on the character. That way you will never be truly sure if the 'demon' riding you is not only you mental problem in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T09:09:32-08:00","id":1061261,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Whispers </b><br /> <br /> I modeled Whispers on the Fettered manifestation largely because when you read the text from Inferno, Whispers behaves like what would become Fettered in CofD. As such one condition goes on the Entity, which alters the Entities capabilities, while urged goes on the Victim, to represent the influence the being is exerting. I admit the way it plays reveals more meta knowledge than you might want, but most of the Condition system involves giving the players access to more meta knowledge, so it didn't seem outside the bounds of the system mechanics. As always, Your Mileage may Vary.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Malpraxis</b><br /> <br /> Re-aligning Malpraxis to 2nd Edition has been challenging. In my current write up, it doesn't have much more mechanical weight than most other Anchors. But in Inferno, a fair amount of word count went into explaining the interplay between Vices and Keys. My alternate idea was to have Vice and Key as separate anchors - recovering a point of Willpower where vice applies, but recovering full Willpower when Vice &amp; Key apply. Any feedback on this would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Maeltinet of the Manor</b><br /> <br /> Here is the writeup of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's proposal. This uses my first draft of Infernal Entities as my guideline. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bleakwood </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The entity that calls itself \u201cBleakwood\u201d inhabits the sprawling Harris Estate on the outskirts of town. It is the spirit of the manor that housed generations of the wealthy Harris family, but has corrupted by the depravity of a cabal of sorcerers that has taken up residence on the Estate. The entity has grown powerful on torment and pain inflicted for its own sake, and has grown into a \u201cMaeltinet\u201d, a servant of a greater infernal entity known as \u201cThurifuge\u2019\u201d.<br /> When Bleakwood manifests, it appears as a giant emaciated corpse with eight arms and four faces. Its body is wrapped in sickly ivy and dead leaves and produces the creaks and groans of a house settling when it moves.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Infernal, Immundi, Maeltinet]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 12, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 24, <b>Size</b> 12, <b>Initiative</b> 22, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Malpraxis: </b> Sadism committed on the Estate grounds. <br /> <b>Influence:</b> The Estate 3, Torment 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot knowingly act against the Harris Family; <b>Bane:</b> Ritually purified bones of a Harris Family member<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Possess, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Essence Thief, Hallucination, <b><i>Know Soul</i></b>, Left-Handed Spanner, Telekinesis, <b><i>Twilight Abduction</i></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Know Soul:</i></b> As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.146)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Twilight Abduction:</i></b> The entity can attempt to drag victims within one yard into an incorporeal state, allowing it to freely interact with the target. Spend three Essence points, and roll the entities\u2019 (Power + Finesse) .The target resists with a roll of (Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance). If the entity wins, shadows drag the victim and his worn possessions through a sudden imploding tear in space. In an instant, the rift closes, and the victim enters Twilight for one hour per remaining success.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T14:58:32-08:00","id":1061346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1061261#post1061261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Malpraxis</b><br /> <br /> Re-aligning Malpraxis to 2nd Edition has been challenging. In my current write up, it doesn't have much more mechanical weight than most other Anchors. But in Inferno, a fair amount of word count went into explaining the interplay between Vices and Keys. My alternate idea was to have Vice and Key as separate anchors - recovering a point of Willpower where vice applies, but recovering full Willpower when Vice &amp; Key apply. Any feedback on this would be appreciated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would treat Keys as <i>second</i> ways to get Willpower - or even Essence for Infernal. You can go after Vice, after Key or after both. I remember in <b>Inferno </b>there were Erynies as examples Infernal demons - they would be about Retribution and Envy. Not many possible ways to play both those archetypes, but you can even see some 'good' in story for use being that brings retribution, yes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-11-2017, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:03:18-08:00","id":1061409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1061261#post1061261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Whispers </b><br /> <br /> I modeled Whispers on the Fettered manifestation largely because when you read the text from Inferno, Whispers behaves like what would become Fettered in CofD. As such one condition goes on the Entity, which alters the Entities capabilities, while urged goes on the Victim, to represent the influence the being is exerting. I admit the way it plays reveals more meta knowledge than you might want, but most of the Condition system involves giving the players access to more meta knowledge, so it didn't seem outside the bounds of the system mechanics. As always, Your Mileage may Vary.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Malpraxis</b><br /> <br /> Re-aligning Malpraxis to 2nd Edition has been challenging. In my current write up, it doesn't have much more mechanical weight than most other Anchors. But in Inferno, a fair amount of word count went into explaining the interplay between Vices and Keys. My alternate idea was to have Vice and Key as separate anchors - recovering a point of Willpower where vice applies, but recovering full Willpower when Vice &amp; Key apply. Any feedback on this would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: The Maeltinet of the Manor</b><br /> <br /> Here is the writeup of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> 's proposal. This uses my first draft of Infernal Entities as my guideline. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Bleakwood </b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The entity that calls itself \u201cBleakwood\u201d inhabits the sprawling Harris Estate on the outskirts of town. It is the spirit of the manor that housed generations of the wealthy Harris family, but has corrupted by the depravity of a cabal of sorcerers that has taken up residence on the Estate. The entity has grown powerful on torment and pain inflicted for its own sake, and has grown into a \u201cMaeltinet\u201d, a servant of a greater infernal entity known as \u201cThurifuge\u2019\u201d.<br /> When Bleakwood manifests, it appears as a giant emaciated corpse with eight arms and four faces. Its body is wrapped in sickly ivy and dead leaves and produces the creaks and groans of a house settling when it moves.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Infernal, Immundi, Maeltinet]<br /> Power 12, Finesse 10, Resistance 12, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 24, <b>Size</b> 12, <b>Initiative</b> 22, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 22<br /> <b>Malpraxis: </b> Sadism committed on the Estate grounds.<br /> <b>Influence:</b> The Estate 3, Torment 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot knowingly act against the Harris Family; <b>Bane:</b> Ritually purified bones of a Harris Family member<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Fetter, Possess, Materialize, Twilight Form, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Dement, Essence Thief, Hallucination, <b><i>Know Soul</i></b>, Left-Handed Spanner, Telekinesis, <b><i>Twilight Abduction</i></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b><i>Know Soul:</i></b> As the Dread Power of the same name (CofD, pg.146)<br /> <br /> <b><i>Twilight Abduction:</i></b> The entity can attempt to drag victims within one yard into an incorporeal state, allowing it to freely interact with the target. Spend three Essence points, and roll the entities\u2019 (Power + Finesse) .The target resists with a roll of (Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance). If the entity wins, shadows drag the victim and his worn possessions through a sudden imploding tear in space. In an instant, the rift closes, and the victim enters Twilight for one hour per remaining success.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much, this was just the sort of thing I was looking for, just couldn't visualize it. Especially the Size.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T23:18:34-08:00","id":1061459,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>RE: Malpraxis Notes</b><br /> <br /> That becomes the tricky part. An Infernal whose Key is a type of Action or Behavior (such as Betrayal or Retribution) is relatively easy to adjudicate. Typically, an anchor rewards the character with willpower when they take some type of action, but how would regain will power if their Key is something passive? (Such as elements (fire, water, iron), time period (days, nights, Mondays), locations ( forests, hospitals,graveyards), and other passive conditions.)</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 03-12-2017, 03:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T00:19:53-08:00","id":1061464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1061459#post1061459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Typically, an anchor rewards the character with willpower when they take some type of action, but how would regain will power if their Key is something passive? (Such as elements (fire, water, iron), time period (days, nights, Mondays), locations ( forests, hospitals,graveyards), and other passive conditions.)</span></div> </div> </div> </div>By being in the enviorment by whole scene / hour, even if it's not opitmal to it. That mean that water demon will stick to water, dark spirit of forest will run to forest itself and demon on Mondays will try to be always summoned on Mondays.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T07:21:43-07:00","id":1061536,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Infernal Entities </b><br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback. A Willpower point gained passively per scene is a bit fast for the system as is (most ephemerals can only gain a point of Willpower passively at a rate of 1/day). However, this consideration has given me some insight into how to make the Malpraxis a bit more mechanically defined. I am posting my revisions below. updated text has been highlighted. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Infernal Entities (Diaboli &amp;Dominions)</b></span><br /> <b>Rank: </b>Dominions run the full range of Ranks. Ephemeral Entities that become Diaboli retain their Rank. Corrupted Ghosts become <i>Larvals</i>, Corrupted Goetia become <i>Deceptors</i> and Corrupted Spirits become <i>Immundi</i>.<br /> <b>Native: </b>Dominions are native to a ream called the Inferno (or simply \u201cHell\u201d)<b>. </b>Corrupted Ephemeral entities retain their ties to their original realms (if any).<br /> <b>Virtue/Vice: </b><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">As creatures of pure sinfulness<b>, </b>Infernal Entities have a Vice, but do not have a Virtue. Instead, they have a Key, which is an additional condition or circumstance of when, where, or how the Vice is expressed. This combination of Vice and Key is the Infernal Entities <i>Malpraxis</i>. The entities Key also defines a <i>Resonant</i> Condition the entity can benefit from for the purposes of regaining essence. Infernal Entities regain up to 1 Willpower point per scene by either fulfilling their Vice, and regain all spent Willpower by fulfilling their <i>Malpraxis</i>, but can only do so once per chapter. Infernal Entities can benefit from being in the presence of individuals fulfilling their Vice or Malpraxis as it had fulfilled it itself. Infernal Entities of Rank 3 gain an additional Vice or Malpraxis, and another at rank 5.</span><br /> <b>Language: </b>Diaboli and Dominions understand all languages, including dead languages or languages used by other supernatural entities. In addition, Diaboli and Dominions speak \u201cDragons Tongue\u201d; a twisted glossolalia that is spoken and understood by the Infernal Entities, but cannot otherwise be translated or deciphered.<br /> <b>Integrity: </b>Diaboli and Dominions don\u2019t have an Integrity trait.<br /> <b>Influences: </b>Diaboli and Dominions have Influences that <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">relate to the Vice and Key their Malpraxis,</span> with Diaboli often retain influences they possessed before their corruption.<br /> <b>Essence: </b>Infernal Entities require the Corrupt Condition in order to regain Essence and prevent Essence Bleed.<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">In addition, Infernal Entities can make use of Resonant Conditions tied to the Vice and Key of their Malpraxis in the same fashion. Diaboli retain the Anchor (Larvae) or Resonant (Immundi) Conditions they possessed prior to their corruption.</span> Diabolists sacrificing precious resources (metaphorical or literal), animals, or even humans to the Infernal Entity in its presence allow it to regain the Resources value of the item or animal, or the current Integrity of a human sacrifice, as Essence.<br /> <b>Secrets &amp; Lies: </b>No supernatural ability can reveal a Diaboli or Dominions lies, half-truths and other deceptions for what they are. Anyone using the power will see the result the Infernal Entity wants them to see. Likewise, no supernatural ability can read the mind or intrude upon the thoughts of an Infernal Entity.<br /> <b>Soul of Sin:</b> Infernal Entities have the <i>Know Soul</i> Numina (the same as the Dread Power).</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-31T10:27:45-07:00","id":1071314,"title":"","content":"I would like to add the ghost you posted <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1061338-how-would-you-build-this-ghost-in-2ed?p=1061462#post1061462\"><b>here</b></a>. You might wanted to add his Curse Numen to the original post.<br /> <br /> What do you think of these new Numina? I am thinking of giving some of them to Bill Cipher, but I don't know if they would work for other entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Piercing Sight:</b> The entity possesses a sixth sense for active supernatural phenomena. It mimics Peripheral Mage Sight, and when alerted, it may roll its Finesse to know the approximate direction and distance of the effect that triggered this Numen. In addition, the entity may see past supernatural means of concealmeant and deceit, and into auras. In both cases, it spends 1 Essence and rolls a Clash Of Wills of Finesse + Rank. Success means the entity sees what is underneath, but doesn't cancel the opponent's effect. When seeing into auras, it mimics the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but does not suffer the Drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Far Sight:</b> The entity may project its senses to other locations as if it had the Clairvoyance Supernatural Merit, but does not suffer dice penalties. It spends 1 Essence as an instant action and rolls Finesse + Rank. This may be combined with other Numina that enhance its senses or communication, such as Piercing Sight, Gauntlet Vision, Seek or Telepathy. If the location has the Open Condition, the entity may combine this with any Numina and Influences by spending 1 willpower point. Locations that have been Warded with the entity's Bane are immune to this Numen.<br /> <br /> <b>Teleportation:</b> The entity may vanish and reappear at another location within line of sight reflexively by spending 1 Essence. If the entity has the Seek Numen, it may teleport to the nearest location with a suitable Condition by spending 3 Essence.<br /> <br /> <b>Weather Control:</b> Possessed only by entities of of Rank 3+, this Numen allows them to impose an Environmental Tilt over an area up to [the highest between Power and Resistance x 100] in yards by spending 3 Essence and rolling Power + Rank. As a guideline, the Tilt has an intensity equal to Successes (caps at the entity's Rank), and may be controled through Influences. While easier for some entities than investing 4+ dots into an Influence, this Numen is not as potent: it always fades at the end of the scene. This Numen only creates one type of Environmental Tilt, but may be purchased multipled times.<br /> <br /> <b>Animal Mask:</b> The entity may disquise itself as an animal by spending 1 Essence, and usually does so when Materializing. As a guideline, entities possess general categories of animals they can transform into equal to their Rank + 1. Canines, birds, arthropods, ungulates, fishes and reptiles are acceptable examples, but not carnivores or vertebrates. Since the entity does not actually have internal organs, it does not gain any special abilities the animal would have (such as the echolocation of a bat, the tracking of a wolf or the poison of a snake). Any natural weaponry deals +0L at most, and no natural armor is acquired (though other Numina and Influences may change this). The maximum Size is Power + Resistance. Despite these limitations, this is useful as a disguise: the entity moves and looks just like a mundane animal to casual observation, but keeps its traits and powers.<br /> <br /> <b>Enduring:</b> In addition to downgrading lethal damage into bashing when Manifest, the entity also downgrades aggravated damage to lethal, even if the source is supernatural. This does not apply against Banes.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardian:</b> Entities with this Numen must have the Fetter Manifestation. The entity can use its Numina and Influences on other targets while Fettered, and the Fetter gains the entity's Rank to all rolls for Perception and contesting supernatural powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 04-02-2017, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-08T08:42:35-07:00","id":1075139,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Numina </b><br /> <br /> These are very good Numina. I revised the mechanics of a few of them for my own uses. I am posting my versions below.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Occult Sight</b>: The entity is sensitive to supernatural phenomena. The entity notices the active use of supernatural abilities within the range of its senses and may make a Finesse roll to approximate its distance and direction. In addition, by spending a point of Essence, it can see through powers of concealment, illusion and deceit with a Clash of Wills using its Rank as its die pool. Lastly, it may mimic the Aura Reading Supernatural Merit, but without drawback.<br /> <br /> <b>Teleportation:</b> When the entity moves, it may reflexively spend 1 Essence to vanish and reappear at another location within its line of sight up to its (Rank x Speed) in yards away. Doing so adds +2 to its Defense for the turn. If the entity has the Seek Numen, it may teleport to the nearest location with a suitable Condition by spending 3 Essence. The entity can spend an additional 2 points of Essence to take a passenger with them (an unwilling passage may resist with a roll of Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Tolerance).<br /> <br /> <b>Weather Control:</b> Typically possessed by entities of Rank 3+, this Numen allows the entity to summon a brief but powerful weather storm. The Numen costs 3 Essence to activate. If successful, the entity may impose an Environmental Tilt over an area with a radius of up to [Power x 100] yards until the end of the scene. This area is treated as an Intensity 2 Extreme Environment. An exceptional success creates an Intensity 3 Extreme Environment instead. The entity may use their Influence to further augment the weather storm\u2019s size, duration and Intensity (where appropriate). This Numen only creates one type of Environmental Tilt, but may be purchased multiple times.</span> <hr /><b>RE: Magath</b><br /> <br /> I had some fun with this. I added second axis that represented more material phenomena, so when you combine them to get some appropriately odd spirit concepts.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> 1- Cats<br /> 2- Dogs<br /> 3- Birds<br /> 4- Snakes<br /> 5- Wasps<br /> 6- Spiders<br /> 7- Ants<br /> 8- Beetles<br /> 9- Air<br /> 10- Earth<br /> 11- Fire<br /> 12- Water<br /> 13- Metal<br /> 14- Wood<br /> 15- Electricity<br /> 16- Light<br /> 17- Darkness<br /> 18- Sword<br /> 19- Gun<br /> 20- Hammer<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> posting a few below <hr /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Green Wild</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The entity known as \u201cGreen Wild\u201d is a plant spirit fused with the essence of unfettered freedom, creating a <i>Magath</i> that draws its essence from the growth of plant life, the more untamed and rampant the better. It uses its power to make plants unnaturally verdant, causing frightening amounts of havoc as the unchecked growth wreck structures and overrun animal life. The spirit is gleeful and obsessive about its work, and even greets opposition and setbacks with a manic enthusiasm. The spirit appears as a constantly shifting mass of roots, leaves, branches, and brambles.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Magath, Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 7, Resistance 9, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 16, <b>Defense</b> 7, <b>Speed</b> 24<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Plants 3, Freedom 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Loses all Willpower if captured or imprisoned; <b>Bane: </b>Petrified Wood<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Gauntlet Breach, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Blast (thorns), Pathfinder, Regenerate</span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Skinning Glare</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">Some years ago, a drug runner turned informant was captured by his former associates. As punishment, strips of flesh were peeled from his body and face, and he was abandoned in the expanse of the desert, left to die beneath the merciless summer sun. Sprits feasted upon his pain, giving rise to a spirit of light that has grown strong from the suffering of being skinned alive - the Magath named \u201cSkinning Glare\u201d. It now roams the expanse of the southwestern desert, flaying and burning anything in its path capable of feeling pain. The Skinning Glare appears as a dark skinned man whose flesh has been torn away in dozens of places. Rather than blood or viscera, these wounds bleed radiant, blinding light.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Magath, Spirit]<br /> Power 7, Finesse 4, Resistance 3, Willpower 7 Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 8, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 7, <b>Defense</b> 4, <b>Speed</b> 21<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Sunlight 2, Suffering 2<br /> <b>Ban:</b> cannot manifest from dusk until dawn; <b>Bane: </b>Aloe<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blast (Flaying Light), Emotional Aura, Strike Blind*</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Strike Blind: </b>The entity using this Numen may blind people over an area, whether using darkness or blinding light (chosen when gained and appropriate to the entity in question). Activating the Numen requires 1 Essence and affects an area with a radius of the entity\u2019s Power in yards, causing the Blinded Tilt. Characters may resist with Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance. The effect is magical in origin but can be dealt with in mundane fashion, such as by activating light sources to partially negate darkness or a welder\u2019s mask to help reduce blinding glare. The Tilt lasts until the entity dismisses it, leaves the area, or the scene ends.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Whispersting</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">The strange entity known as \u201cWhispersting\u201d is a Wasp spirit that feeds on secrets. It is an aggressive hunter, seeking creatures that hold compromising or dangerous secrets. It ravages the mind of the secret holders, devouring their thoughts and memories. Having consumed the secret thoughts of many creatures has made Whispersting clever, inhumanly intelligent, treacherous and utterly mad. It appears as a large swarm of dark blue wasps with glowing eyes and oddly wrinkled thoraxes.<br /> <b>Rank</b> 3[Magath, Spirit]<br /> Power 9, Finesse 9, Resistance 5, Willpower 10 Essence 20<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 12, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 14, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 28<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Secrets 2, Wasps 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot manifest in the presence of sapient creatures with Intelligence or Wits 1; <b>Bane: </b>Lead<br /> <b>Manifestation: </b>Discorporate, Materialize, Reaching, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Curse (Amnesia)*, Dement, Pierce Mind*, Seek, Swarm Form*,<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013</b> <b>Curse: </b>The entity curses a target with a specific malady. An entity can typically only inflict one type of affliction, but examples include boils, disease, madness, spiritual malaise, and many others. The Numen costs 3 Essence, and the activation roll is contested by the victim\u2019s Stamina or Resolve + Supernatural Tolerance. If the entity succeeds, in may impose a Condition or Tilt appropriate to its particular curse (such as Amnesia, Blind, Deafened, Madness, Mute, or Sick). The entity can also specify an outward sign of the Curse; typically a type of disfigurement, marking or scar. The Curse remains until the entity either removes it or is destroyed. Certain supernatural means may also be able to remove the curse.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Pierce Mind: </b>As the Dread Power of the same name (Werewolf: the Forsaken 2nd Edition, pg. 211)<br /> <br /> <b>Numina - Swarm Form</b>: This Numen allows a spirit to break up its body into thousands of tiny parts. By spending 2 points of Essence, the Spirit disintegrates into a mass of discrete size 1 or less parts (such as a mass of whirling razors or swarm of stinging insects). This Swarm can then be directed focus its attack on a single target (in which case the target suffers bashing damage every turn equal to the entities Rank; this may be increased to lethal by spending 2 Essence), or spread out over the area, creating the <i>Swarm</i> Tilt with a radius in yards equal to the Entities Rank.</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 04-08-2017, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-27T18:45:35-07:00","id":1084807,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Four Horsemen</b><br /> <br /> Here are a few new entities. I was playing with the imagery of the &quot;Four Horsemen of the Apocalypse&quot;, so I developed several power ghosts that fit into the archetype. <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Specter of Blight</b></span><br /> The Specter of Blight on remembers vague details of its mortal life; she remembers a humble life as a farmer\u2019s wife until a brutal famine ravaged her village until she perished from starvation (along with most of the rest of her village). She haunted her hovel until it burned to the ground many years later. But the ghost has held on to her hunger and despair until it became part of her nature. The Specter of Blight appears as an emaciated woman with thin red hair and of inhuman height, dressed in rags and wrapped in a dusty grey shawl.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Ghost]<br /> Power 10 Finesse 10, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 7, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Perseverance, <b>Vice</b> Ravenous<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Spread Starvation<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Survival<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Stillness<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Hunger 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Will honor a request from someone that has fasted for 7 days<br /> <b>Bane:</b> sprouted barley, anointed with tears<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Discorporate, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Blight*, Drain, Emotional Aura (Despair), Entropic Decay, Essence Thief, Seek<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina - Blight: </b>The entity can destroy a crop of food within a radius equal to 100 yards per point of Power. The Numen costs seven Essence to activate. On a success, the crop fails, afflicted with a sudden, crippling blight that kills the plants overnight, leaving not a single grain or piece of fruit edible</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Specter of Calamity</b></span><br /> It is believed The Specter of Calamity was once an individual that worked closely with the dead (most likely a priest or a mortician). His life ended in a freak mishap (slipped while stepping out of the tub), and his Ghost lingered on, both angered and amused by the grotesque meaninglessness of it all. It is now a potent entity that has tied itself to Death from Misfortune. The Specter wanders the Underworld (and occasionally the lands of the living), devouring the Ghosts of those slain by accidents, freak occurrences and misadventure. The Specter of Calamity appears as a skeletal figure dressed in a black cassock and sporting a wide-brimmed black hat. The Ghost is talkative and knowledgeable, and has a wry sense of humor.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Ghost]<br /> Power 10 Finesse 12, Resistance 8, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 13, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 27<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Insightful, <b>Vice</b> Bitter<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Consume the Ghosts of those slain by Misfortune<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Occult<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Chance<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Misfortune 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot refuse if challenged to a game of chance<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Shards the grave marker of someone who died of old age<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Discorporate, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Smite), Fate Sense, Seek, Telekinesis, Telepathy*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina - Telepathy: </b>Entities with this Numen can reach out and link their minds with others, allowing instantaneous and reliable communication. The spirit rolls Power + Finesse. If resisted, subtract the target\u2019s Resolve + Supernatural Advantage. If the target is mortal, they gain the <i>Shaken</i> Condition - being that intimate with an alien mind is profoundly disturbing.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Specter of Carnage</b></span><br /> The Specter of Carnage is a Ghost that was once a soldier who served on of the great European powers during the 17<sup>th</sup> century, and descended into the underworld when his medals and decorations become lost over time. Since that time he has become a creature anchored to the brutality of warfare; a wraith of broken bodies and burned flesh. The Specter of Carnage is a giant figure wrapped in barbed wire and dressed in a tattered uniform and adorned with a mismatched assortment of combat equipment used in the centuries since his death. His face is skeletal with fire in the pits of his eyes and breathes a ghastly yellow vapor.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Ghost]<br /> Power 12 Finesse 8, Resistance 10, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 18, <b>Size</b> 8, <b>Initiative</b> 18, <b>Defense</b> 10, <b>Speed</b> 28<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Duty, <b>Vice</b> Brutal<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To Indulge in Warfare</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Remembrance:</b> Firearms<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Blood<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Violence 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must abide by the terms of a truce or cease fire<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A Bayonet over 100 years old that has taken a life.<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Discorporate, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Blast (Machinegun), Dement, Phantom Arsenal*, Regenerate, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span></span> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Specter of Epidemic</b></span><br /> The Specter of Epidemic is the lingering shade of an individual whose final days were spent in agony as a virulent infection ravaged their body. The ghost that rose haunted the hospital until it was exorcised and sent into the underworld. Over the years, it rose in influence among other ghosts that lost their lives to disease. It now leads a bizarre \u201cplague cult\u201d among the dead. It has now turned its attention to sharing its vision with the living. The Specter of Epidemic sports a white laboratory coat and wears a plaque doctor\u2019s mask. Any exposed flesh is riddled with pox scars and seeping sores.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 4[Ghost]<br /> Power 9 Finesse 9, Resistance 12, Willpower 10, Essence 25<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 17, <b>Size</b> 5, <b>Initiative</b> 20, <b>Defense</b> 9, <b>Speed</b> 25<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Zeal, <b>Vice</b> Spite<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> Spread Infectious Disease<br /> <b>Remembrance:</b> Medicine<br /> <b>Innate Key:</b> Key of Disease<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Disease 4<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Cannot harm a person who recovered from being gravely ill with an infectious disease<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Ritually purified Salt mixed with the ashes of a cremated victim of disease<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Discorporate, Fetter, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Aggressive Meme, Heal*, Implant Mission, Mortal Mask, Plague Bearer*, Regenerate<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Numina - Heal: </b>The entity can heal others\u2019 wounds, typically for a hefty price. This Numen costs 1 Essence and a Power+ Finesse roll to activate. Each success heals a level of bashing damage, while two successes can heal a point of lethal damage. The lethal damage healed can be used to mend aggravated damage, but each point of aggravated damage cured costs three additional points of Essence. This power may also be used to fight off disease or the effects of poison \u2014 each success adding to the subjects\u2019 resistance rolls on a one-to-one basis.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Plague Bearer: </b>An entity with this Numen can inflict disease upon a mortal creature. This Numen costs three Essence. The activation roll is contested by the victim\u2019s Resolve + Stamina + Supernatural Tolerance. On a success, the victim suffers from a potentially fatal disease and gains the Sick (Grave) tilt. What the disease is, and whether it\u2019s infectious is up to the Storyteller, but it\u2019s always potentially fatal. If the disease is not terminal and incurable, it should take at least a number of successes equal to the greater of the entities Power or Resistance on an extended Stamina + Resolve roll to beat, with one roll allowed per week.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":".  Updated to Geist 2nd Edition Rules 01-20-2019, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-01T14:10:27-07:00","id":1110348,"title":"","content":"Do you think you could create some Abyssals using the ideas from <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/925972-2e-abyssal-aspects-and-numina\"><b>this thread</b></a>?<br /> <br /> Do you have any guidelines for determining the Rank of a given entity before writing their stats?<br /> <br /> I wrote <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/349384-think-of-fictional-characters-and-say-what-they-would-be-in-cofd?p=1109096#post1109096\"><b>Bill Cipher</b></a> as an ephemeral being, with the help of some of your homebrew. What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T13:57:36-07:00","id":1110651,"title":"","content":"Its been a little bit since I've been in my Chronicles of Darkness headspace (blame Shadowrun and Exalted!), but lets take a look at these questions.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Abyssal Entities</b><br /> I have not taken a hard look at abyssal entities yet, since I haven't had the opportunity to run a Mage game where they would be most relevant. But the mechanics in the posted thread offer alot of good ideas for how to approach them in a way that makes them feel distinct from other Ephemeral types. I will post anything I come up with from my explorations.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Entity Rank Guidelines</b><br /> I start with concept - the basic idea of what the Entity is,what it does, and what role it plays in the story. After that I look at how much of an obstacle the entity should present if you use it in a game. A rank 1 entity is a minor nuisance that could be resolved in a session, while a Rank 4 or 5 may take an entire story arc to deal with. After that I write out the creature at the rank that feels most appropriate. Then I will give it another pass and see if I can get away with getting the same feel at a slightly lower rank. I do this because (at least for me),it more interesting to create entities that can challenge the players in ways other than overwhelming them with raw power. When using an entity I always try to remember the capabilities of the characters- a Rank 2 Spirit is an almost trivial opponent for Werewolves,but can be a deadly threat to Mortals or other creatures without the tools to handle spirits. And never be afraid to adjust on the fly, its the entity to too much (or not strong enough) for the challenge you intended,but add or subtract a few dice or health boxes.<br /> <br /> <b>RE: Bill </b><br /> This is quite excellent!I especially like the use use of Price of Power as a Numina. About the only thing I might change is one of his Bans -Bills most telling defeats were while possessing someones mind - perhaps he is vulnerable to Astral Combat? I rather like the idea that in the arena where he is at his strongest is also when he is at his most vulnerable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":775,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","user":"Reighnhell","date":". 06-15-2018, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T06:13:07-07:00","id":1112627,"title":"","content":"Would you consider a spirit of sex and death to be a Magath?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-07T15:27:51-07:00","id":1112956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1112627#post1112627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you consider a spirit of sex and death to be a Magath?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends. It's a rape/murder spirit? Then it's a particular kind of murder spirit. Is it a morbid emotional spirit that was spawned by the sheer biological need to transcend death?<br /> <br /> The permutations are practically endless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T14:14:24-07:00","id":1113370,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Sex &amp; Death</b><br /> <br /> As noted above, there are many permutations on this theme. My inclination would be to create the spirit as a conceptually &quot;pure&quot; Spirit - the realtionship between sexuality and mortality is a old enough and resonant enough concept that it would likely spawn spirits that would not be considered Magath. At least as I interpret the concept, a &quot;Magath&quot; are spirits that embody &quot;illogical&quot; combinations or unprecedented concepts. So while a &quot;Sex and Death&quot; spirit would probably not be a Magath, a &quot;Sex and Stone&quot; or a &quot;Death and Appliances&quot; spirit would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T15:27:44-07:00","id":1113417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1113370#post1113370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Sex &amp; Death</b> &quot;Death and Appliances&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Death by Appliances</i> would be so pissed at you calling it an unnatural spirit hybrid.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T16:06:50-07:00","id":1113436,"title":"","content":"Reighnhell, have you ever experimented with combining Numina and Influences, allowing improved versions of Numina and Influences for entities of higher Rank, and giving unique Numina/Influences to certain entities?<br /> <br /> For example: Aggressive Meme + Sign + Influence Computers 3 creates a very powerful computer virus with an audio-visual component. Firestater + Implant Mission + Influence Fire 3 creates a fire that obeys simple commands without constant input from the entity instead of spreading wildly, essentially creating a temporary Rank 1 fire spirit. Blast + Entropic Decay results in a ranged attack that only harms non-living targets.<br /> <br /> For advanced uses of Numina and Influences, I house rule that by spending additional Essence and/or Willpower points, entities of sufficient power can unlock new features, such as giving 8 Again on an Influence roll (including Clash Of Wills), unleashing Blasts that bend around Cover, an Implant Mission that gives 8 Again and so on.<br /> <br /> For unique Numina/Influences, do you prefer altering canon ones or coming up with new ones wholesale? Sometimes an entity has powers that simply don't match the more broad sort of effects represented by normal Numina/Influences. For example: how would one represent the following powers?<br /> <br /> 1) Transforming 3D beings into 2D and vice versa?<br /> 2) Being supernaturally skilled at certain mundane tasks?<br /> 3) Being in many places at the same time?<br /> 4) Creating a pocket realm where you have control over certain physical laws, such as the flow of time and the pull/intensity of gravity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-08T16:32:08-07:00","id":1113449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1113370#post1113370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least as I interpret the concept, a &quot;Magath&quot; are spirits that embody &quot;illogical&quot; combinations or unprecedented concepts. So while a &quot;Sex and Death&quot; spirit would probably not be a Magath, ... a &quot;Death and Appliances&quot; spirit would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps not for much longer, if accidental death trends and warning labels are any indications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-09T02:30:06-07:00","id":1113662,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Combined Numina/Influence</b><br /> <br /> I haven't played much in this space, but I would likely have the Entity spend a point of willpower to &quot;stunt&quot; one of its existing abilities to create the desired effect. For special tricks or advanced abilities, this feels like an elegant and flexible approach.<br /> <br /> <b>Re: Unique Numina</b><br /> <br /> I like using a variety of techniques when crafting something unique for the entity in question. I like trying to find a System Precedent - some place where the effect I am looking for as already been modeled. If I find something good, I rework it until it fits mechanically into the Numina framework and is roughly on par with the published Numina. If I can't find something pre-existing , I will build the power from the ground up. So to use your examples -<br /> <br /> 1) <i>Transforming 3D beings into 2D and vice versa</i> - This would need to be a new Numina. The first thing is to do some reading to see if the effect has been done before. The big advantages to being 2 Dimensional would be for Defense and Stealth. A +2 bonus to Defense and Stealth sounds fair , as well as allowing narrative effects such as slipping under doors or disguising themselves as drawings. Since this seems like something that can be inflicted on others, I would let the Power+Finesse roll to be contested.<br /> <br /> 2) <i>Being supernaturally skilled at certain mundane tasks.</i> This could be represented by a new Numina, but it would be easier to just add the entities rank to skill rolls relevant to Entity. Combined with a spirits typically higher die pools, this should be good for representing the Entities talents. No sense in gilding the lily.<br /> <br /> 3) <i>Being Many Places at Once. </i>Another that would require a New Numina. This can be problematic, as any character able to make multiple copies of themselves is a situation almost begging to be abused. But a rough idea would be a Numina that would allow the Entity to exist in multiple locations - they would be able to exist in [Rank+1] locations. The entity could perceive the events of each location,and even act independently at each location. Doing this is distraction and the entity would suffer a penalty to their actions. The also entity would have a single health track - attacks from locations where the entity is co-located is applied to that single health track normally.<br /> <br /> <i>4) Creating a Pocket Realm.</i> New Numina -this would grant the Entity [Rank] dots in the Safe Place Merit. While inside their pocket realm, the Entity would have the equivalent of Influence 5 (Pocket Realm Environment). i would also restrict this to Entities of rank 4 or higher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T10:47:33-07:00","id":1120897,"title":"","content":"Can ghosts in the CoD-Verse form away from the places they died? I was thinking of statting up the ghost/time-lost Vietnam Era Marine Platoon from the Hellblazer story &quot;When Johnny Comes Marching Home&quot; as Rank 1 or 2 Ghosts and posting it here for comment. They all probably died in Vietnam, but manifest in their old hometown, summoned by family members fervently praying for their return even 20 years later. I wanted to see if that could work in the CoD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:11:46-07:00","id":1120910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1120897#post1120897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can ghosts in the CoD-Verse form away from the places they died? I was thinking of statting up the ghost/time-lost Vietnam Era Marine Platoon from the Hellblazer story &quot;When Johnny Comes Marching Home&quot; as Rank 1 or 2 Ghosts and posting it here for comment. They all probably died in Vietnam, but manifest in their old hometown, summoned by family members fervently praying for their return even 20 years later. I wanted to see if that could work in the CoD</div> </div> </div> </div>If those form their Anchors, probably? I don't think Ghosts can teleport between Anchors anymore, but if one forms and all their Anchors are located elsewhere...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:23:11-07:00","id":1120988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1120910#post1120910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If those form their Anchors, probably? I don't think Ghosts can teleport between Anchors anymore, but if one forms and all their Anchors are located elsewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving them a Manifestation that allows them said teleportation seems trivial enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T22:20:04-07:00","id":1121195,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Ghosts</b><br /> <br /> I have always run it that the geographic location of where a person dies isn't always important. One might be bound to the location of its death, while another might appear wandering the halls of his home, even though they died at a hospital miles away. Its the sort of thing I like leaving ambiguous so a Occult minded player can pick at the mystery of it all.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T00:47:15-07:00","id":1121219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1120910#post1120910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If those form their Anchors, probably? I don't think Ghosts can teleport between Anchors anymore, but if one forms and all their Anchors are located elsewhere...</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct, they do however have option to have one of their Manifestations be &quot;Discorperation&quot; and that can thought of as a slow painful teleportation based on how Ephemeral Beings reform...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T01:03:29-07:00","id":1121222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1057309#post1057309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> that's what I was thinking, but it could be that the Spirit is too short-sighted to realize that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends, spirits may have no conscious choice of what Manifestations it possesses and without the ability to Fetter to or Claim a promising activist that's one of it's better options and that's a great choice if it has the Agressive Meme Numena, and as a spirit based on an Ideology it makes a great deal of sense to do so. That turns activists into superaturally turbo charged carriers of that Ideology, thus could account for why Ideological lines seem to be carving the modern world apart, Ideology Spirits are extremely Essense and Rank efficient in creating more of itself (doesn't require Influence 4, and thus Rank 4), and while there are competing Ideologies they less exclusive than emotions (less devouring each other as feelings might seem to do, and more competing for space/limited Essence provided by attention).<br /> <br /> The only better option is to Urge or Claim someone leading a branch of activism for the Ideology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:19:43-07:00","id":1124065,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">Here's the guys from Hellblazer I've been meaning to make. Tell me what you think.<br /> <br /> <b>Soldier of the Lost Platoon</b></span><br /> <br /> <i>A soldier who never made it back to his hometown in middle america. At least, not alive. For him, the war never ended, and he continually relives his last operation before he was killed by a friendly fire bombing called down by his own commanding officer, forever doomed to repeat the same mistakes.</i><b><br /> <br /> Rank:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 1</span><br /> <b>Attributes:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Power 3, Finesse 2, Resistance 3, Willpower 5, Essence 10</span><br /> <b>Initiative:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 5</span><br /> <b>Defense:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 3</span><br /> <b>Speed:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 11</span><br /> <b>Size:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 5</span><br /> <b>Corpus:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 8<br /> <b>Anchor</b>: his grieving parents</span><br /> <b>Influences:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Parents (Theirs) 1</span><br /> <b>Ban:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Must follow the orders of Lieutenant Frank Ross</span><br /> <b>Bane:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Salt</span><br /> <b>Manifestation:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Materialize, Twilight Form</span><br /> <b>Numina:</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> Mortal Mask, Blast (Ghostly M-16), Stalwart</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-30-2017, 09:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T16:49:00-07:00","id":1124083,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: The Lost Platoon</b><br /> <br /> Very solid write up. I myself have also adapted, borrowed and outright stolen ideas from Hellblazer!<br /> <br /> As a personal aside, I have always loved a good ghost story. Sure, you can run ghosts in Monster-of-Week fashion, to be Busted and then forgotten. But you can get some great emotional roleplaying out if you portray them as people - lost, frightened, confused people in desperate need of help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T07:21:11-07:00","id":1135436,"title":"","content":"Writing something for the Story hooks for Kids thread. A Rank 2 Friendship(/dog possibly) spirit that's attached itself to an Elementary School kid as an &quot;imaginary friend&quot;. Trying to make something that's scary enough to make a story but not too frightening to fight for OP's 11 and 7 year old players. Tell me what you think<br /> <br /> <b>Friendship/Dog Spirit: Pack Guardian</b><br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b>: 2<br /> <b>Attributes</b>: Power 6, Finesse 2, Resistance 4, Willpower 6, Essence 15<br /> <b>Initiative</b>: 6<br /> <b>Defense</b>: 2<br /> <b>Speed</b>: 13 (species factor 5)<br /> <b>Size</b>: 3<br /> <b>Corpus</b>: 7<br /> <b>Ban</b>: Cannot harm or betray any child that has befriended it<br /> <b>Bane</b>: Coyotes<br /> <b>Influences</b>: Dogs (OO), Friendships (OO) (sacrificed 2 numina)<br /> <b>Manifestations</b>: Twilight Form, Fetter, Unfetter<br /> <b>Numina</b>: Sign, Telekinesis, Awe (piercing howl)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 09-04-2017, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T08:51:26-07:00","id":1135463,"title":"","content":"The ban is... highly convenient, plus there's no way it'd have 3 dots of influences in dogs whilst being rank 2. The horror factor of canine spirits comes from over-protectiveness. There's an example of a claimed dog by such a spirit that killed a parent for raising their voice at their kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T09:11:29-07:00","id":1135473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1135463#post1135463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ban is... highly convenient, plus there's no way it'd have 3 dots of influences in dogs whilst being rank 2. The horror factor of canine spirits comes from over-protectiveness. There's an example of a claimed dog by such a spirit that killed a parent for raising their voice at their kids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will fix that, but having issues thinking of a good ban","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 08-30-2017, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T18:51:03-07:00","id":1136043,"title":"","content":"You are on the right track.This strikes me as spirit defined by Loyalty and Friendship, so a simple ban of &quot;Cannot Harm or Betray a Child it has befriended&quot; would suit this spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T19:01:40-07:00","id":1136045,"title":"","content":"Define befriended though? I don't think a Friendship spirit can, ironically, ever have a true friendship, because he would just see people's friendship as a way to get Essence. So is it just if the child truly believes the Spirit is his friend?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-31T19:18:36-07:00","id":1136052,"title":"","content":"That is a good point. I think a spirit can recognized &quot;friendship&quot; and other such emotions, but it would always be warped and driven by the drive to gather essence and the frankly alien way such a creature would think. What a human would consider friendship, and what a essence starved alien entity would consider friendship could be very different things. For ease of use , perhaps a subtle shift of the ban's language - &quot;Cannot Harm or Betray a Child that has befriended it&quot; might work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T09:09:53-07:00","id":1138604,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about the Achronals, and how some come from dramatically different environments/times. And how other Ephemerals also might come from dramatically alien domains. But how to represent bring a bit of &quot;home&quot; to the material world?<br /> <br /> What about having a <b>Xenoforming</b> (name recommended to change) Manifestation? Mechanically, it would work like a Beast imposing Lair Trait (Environmental Tilt). Probably require the Open Condition (at least). Instead of the being creating a body for itself, it projects its nature into the environment. Might even add a Genius Loci Manifestation (requiring the Controlled Condition, similar to Possession and Claim) and allowing directed environmental hazards and effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T10:10:47-07:00","id":1138623,"title":"","content":"Could they use this in conjunction with another Manifestation, such Image or Materialize?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:08:59-07:00","id":1138736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138623#post1138623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could they use this in conjunction with another Manifestation, such Image or Materialize?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure? I don't see why not. Sure, some entities might only possess this and Twilight Form, but a Lord of Flame (high Rank fire Spirit) could Materialize a body of fire, and then invoke this to turn the place into an Inferno. Or the other way around.<br /> <br /> I mean, for simple examples like that, there is a lot of overlap with a place being Open to fire like that anyways, but this is basically to mechanically support applying Environment Tilts easier. Or for cases like the Herald of Dim Stars imposing the Freezing Vacuum of the near Heat Death at the end of time without needing Influence: Cold and Vacuum.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-08-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:40:21-07:00","id":1138745,"title":"","content":"Re: Xenoforming<br /> <br /> I like this idea - so I have fiddled with how to represent the idea mechanically. the results are below. <hr /><br /> <b>Nexus Intrusion (Manifestation)</b><br /> (Requires Open Condition) An Entity with this Manifestation can force a portion of an alien and often-hostile environment into the physical world. Entities will typically manifest environments aligned with its nature (such as a Fire Spirit manifesting the Inferno Tilt) .By spending 3 Essence, creates a Level 2 Extreme Environment and applies an Environmental Tilt. Every additional 2points of Essence spent can increase the level of the Extreme Environment by 1 or add an additional Environmental tilt (to a maximum Extreme Environment level or number of Tilts equal to the Entities Rank). The Manifestation lasts until the end of scene.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:41:25-07:00","id":1138746,"title":"","content":"Influences both represents the nature of ephemerals, and are already their method for imposing their natures on their environment. Why switch it up with a Manifestation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T16:58:32-07:00","id":1138749,"title":"","content":"<b>RE: Influnces</b><br /> <br /> You make a good point. But I think the mechanical goal here is to make it possible for even a middling spirit to pull off a stunt that would otherwise require at least Influence 4-5. While I wouldn't give this manifestation to just any spirit, but I think it could prove useful in the right context. And its a good one if you need to add just the right amount of extra challenge to this evenings Spirit Encounter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T20:52:45-07:00","id":1138792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138749#post1138749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>RE: Influnces</b><br /> <br /> You make a good point. But I think the mechanical goal here is to make it possible for even a middling spirit to pull off a stunt that would otherwise require at least Influence 4-5. While I wouldn't give this manifestation to just any spirit, but I think it could prove useful in the right context. And its a good one if you need to add just the right amount of extra challenge to this evenings Spirit Encounter.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd restrict it to rank 3 spirits and above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T21:30:04-07:00","id":1138797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138745#post1138745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Xenoforming<br /> <br /> I like this idea - so I have fiddled with how to represent the idea mechanically. the results are below. <hr /><br /> <b>Nexus Intrusion (Manifestation)</b><br /> (Requires Open Condition) An Entity with this Manifestation can force a portion of an alien and often-hostile environment into the physical world. Entities will typically manifest environments aligned with its nature (such as a Fire Spirit manifesting the Inferno Tilt) .By spending 3 Essence, creates a Level 2 Extreme Environment and applies an Environmental Tilt. Every additional 2points of Essence spent can increase the level of the Extreme Environment by 1 or add an additional Environmental tilt (to a maximum Extreme Environment level or number of Tilts equal to the Entities Rank). The Manifestation lasts until the end of scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't this essentially a more versatile version of the Weather Control Numen?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-08T22:02:12-07:00","id":1138801,"title":"","content":"It's like a Mass Control, sort of, but definitely fits in the same mechanical space as Weather Control.<br /> <br /> I imagine it can materialize not only elemental manifestations, but could for example cause a massive outbreak of rage or sadness, or silence or fear.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-09-2017, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T01:36:33-07:00","id":1138826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138801#post1138801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's like a Mass Control, sort of, but definitely fits in the same mechanical space as Weather Control.<br /> <br /> I imagine it can materialize not only elemental manifestations, but could for example cause a massive outbreak of rage or sadness, or silence or fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Riot environmental tilt for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T04:23:22-07:00","id":1138846,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Nexus Intrusion vs Weather Control </b><br /> <br /> There is definitely thematic overlap between the two. My intent with &quot;Nexus Intrusion&quot; was the idea that the entity super imposes its alien realm onto the world. The manifestation needs the flexibility to accommodate a wide variety of possible environments. My main concern with my first write up is that its not explicit about how much area it covers - I am thinking the effect should be limited to an area surrounding the entity - perhaps Rank x 3 yards. Another adjustment is leaving the Intensity of the Environment to a flat level 2 and only allowing essence to be used to add tilts. That way it still allows a clear benefit to Weather Control (greater area and potentially more intensity).<br /> <hr /><b>Nexus Intrusion v.2 (Manifestation)</b><br /> (Requires Open Condition) An Entity with this Manifestation can force a portion of an alien and often-hostile environment into the physical world. Entities will typically manifest environments aligned with its nature (such as a Fire Spirit manifesting the Inferno Tilt) .By spending 3 Essence, creates a Level 2 Extreme Environment and applies an Environmental Tilt. Every additional 2points of Essence spent can add an additional Environmental tilt (to a maximum number of Tilts equal to the Entities Rank). This effect covers a (Rank x 3 yard) radius centered on the entity.The Manifestation lasts until the end of scene.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T06:14:35-07:00","id":1138867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reighnhell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138846#post1138846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Re: Nexus Intrusion vs Weather Control </b><br /> <br /> There is definitely thematic overlap between the two. My intent with &quot;Nexus Intrusion&quot; was the idea that the entity super imposes its alien realm onto the world. The manifestation needs the flexibility to accommodate a wide variety of possible environments. My main concern with my first write up is that its not explicit about how much area it covers - I am thinking the effect should be limited to an area surrounding the entity - perhaps Rank x 3 yards. Another adjustment is leaving the Intensity of the Environment to a flat level 2 and only allowing essence to be used to add tilts. That way it still allows a clear benefit to Weather Control (greater area and potentially more intensity).<br /> <hr /><b>Nexus Intrusion v.2 (Manifestation)</b><br /> (Requires Open Condition) An Entity with this Manifestation can force a portion of an alien and often-hostile environment into the physical world. Entities will typically manifest environments aligned with its nature (such as a Fire Spirit manifesting the Inferno Tilt) .By spending 3 Essence, creates a Level 2 Extreme Environment and applies an Environmental Tilt. Every additional 2points of Essence spent can add an additional Environmental tilt (to a maximum number of Tilts equal to the Entities Rank). This effect covers a (Rank x 3 yard) radius centered on the entity.The Manifestation lasts until the end of scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about scaling the size to something like the Safe Place Merit(s)? Rank and they both go to 5, and it allows near-gods to affect vaster areas.<br /> <br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> Other fun ideas:<br /> <br /> A powerful ghost with <b>Nexus Intrusion (Zombies!)</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 09-09-2017, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T07:02:22-07:00","id":1138878,"title":"","content":"Re: Scaling Size<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1138867#post1138867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about scaling the size to something like the Safe Place Merit(s)? Rank and they both go to 5, and it allows near-gods to affect vaster areas.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>There are a few limits with using Safe Place as a base. The CofD version of the merit uncouples it from the size and area - it now represent degree of security. Good for keeping out intruders, not so good for determining how much terrain the Safe Place actually covers (the book recommends using equipment to determine the property size). Ideally for the flavor and to keep a leash on the effect, I wouldn't want it to extend much farther than the Open Condition it is based on. I went with Rank x3 yards because that is how far a ghost can travel from its anchor , which seems like a good rough estimate to how far such an area would extend.<br /> <br /> Practically speaking , a rank 5 entity can open a Nexus Intrusion that has a radius of 15 yards/45 feet. Its a decent area - enough to be a hazard for anyone in the vicinity, but not quite enough to end up on the national news. Boosting it to Rank x 5 probably wouldn't break anything either.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T20:40:41-07:00","id":1140415,"title":"","content":"What do you think of these new powers, Reighnhell?<br /> <br /> <b>Conjure Servant:</b> The entity may create minor servants from thin air. These servants must be of the same category of Ephemeral Being and share the purview. Spend 2 Essence and roll Power + Finesse. A Rank 1 servant is created and lasts for one hour per Success, or one day per Success with 1 Willpower. For every 2 additional Essence, increase the servant's Rank by 1, which must be lower than the creator's. Halve the Essence cost if the creator is in its native realm. These servants share the Bans and Banes of their creator, start with Essence equal to their Rank, have full Corpus and a maximum Size of [highest between Power and Resistance x 3]. These servants may be improved, altered and compelled with the creator's Influences. If their creator is destroyed, these servants do not vanish. Any given creator may only have a total amount of Rank dots worth of servants existing equal to its [Rank x 3]. This Numen is limited to entities of Rank 4+.<br /> <br /> <b>Pocket Realm (Requires Open Condition):</b> By spending 5 Essence, the entity transforms an area with a radius equal to [Power x 100] yards into an environment that it can shape at will. This area is considered a Safe Place 5 and while inside the entity has Influence 5 (Pocket Realm) at no Essence cost. This lasts for one day per Success, or one week per Success with 10 Essence. The Pocket Realm can be made permanent with 1 Willpower point if the area is turned into a Verge. The entity may teleport between Pocket Realms once per scene by spending 1 Willpower point. This Numen is limited to entities of Rank 4+, and they can only have Rank + 1 Pocket Realms at any time.<br /> <br /> <b>Mirage:</b> As long as the entity succeeds on a Perception roll, it applies its Defense against ranged attacks. By spending 1 Essence, it may Dodge reflexively. By spending 1 Willpower, it may add its Rank as bonus Success on a Dodge.<br /> <br /> <b>Influence Starter (Reaching):</b> As per Firestarter, but is now defined as the creation of a minor instance of one of the entity's Influences, whatever they are. By spending 1 Essence and rolling Power + Finesse, the entity creates one small instance of one of its purview per Success within Power in yards. Unless further improved with the associated Influence, these only last for the scene. This Numen only has to be purchased once, as it allows the entity to create minor instance of all its Influences. Assume that the Equipment Bonus, Size and Availability of the created instance iare equal to those of a mundane equivalent.<br /> <br /> <b>Open Third Eye:</b> As per Mixed Blessing, but only allows the entity to bestow Supernatural Merits. To compensate, each time this Numen is purchased, the entity may choose [Rank x 3] dots of Supernatural Merits it can bestow, including Advanced and Epic versions, and spends Essence equal to 1/3 of the dots given. The target must be mortal but does not need to meet the prerequisites of the Merits.<br /> <br /> <b>Spark Of Life (Reaching): </b>The entity may bring inanimate objects to life. By spending 1 Essence and rolling Power + Finesse, the object becomes sentient and obeys the commands of the entity, which don't have to be spoken out loud but require direct line of sight. Objects without their own means of locomotion cannot leave their spot, unless the entity spends 2 Essence, which allows the object to levitate up to 10 feet above the ground and move around. Objects have a dice pool for operating themselves equal to the entity's Successes x 2 (maximum dice pool of 10), and remain animate for one hour per Success, or one day per Success with 1 Willpower point. If the entity also has Enchant Object, it may grant Numina and/or Influences to the animated object, which uses its own dice pool for them but needs to receive Essence from the entity.<br /> <br /> <b>Enchant Object:</b> By touching an object and rolling Power + Finesse, the entity may transfer its Numina and/or Influences to it. It must spend 2 Essence per Numen or Influence dot (maximum of Rank x 2 Numina/Influences). This lasts for one hour per Success, or one day per Success with 1 Willpower point. The enchanted object startes with 0 Essence, but may receive Essence from willing entities and hold up to [the Rank of the entity which created it x 5] in Essence. It may also activate its powers with Willpower points, and absorb Essence from something with the Open Condition related to the purview of the entity that created it once per day with a roll of Presence + Wits. If the person using this object breaks any of the entity's Bans or allows the object to be struck with any of the entity&quot;s Banes, the object is destroyed immediately. The entity may have as many Enchanted Objects as its Essence supply will allow, but almost always demands something in return for one.<br /> <br /> <b>Astral Gateway (Abnormal Rank 3+ Goetia Only \u2014 Requires Open Condition):</b> By spending 3 Essence, the entity opens a portal to the Astral that it and other entities may use, applying the \u201cAstral Gate\u201d Condition to the location. The portal only allows the passage of Goetia; for material beings it simply becomes possible to meditate into the Astral, even if they are normally incapable of doing so. [Maybe Goetia of sufficiently high Rank and/or weirdness can have a version of this Manifestation that allows physical entrance into the Astral?]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 09-15-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T01:49:13-07:00","id":1140450,"title":"","content":"Pocket Realm looks like something only rank 5 and above entities should have (unless a ban limits them their usage). Conjure Servant looks like spirit reproduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T15:36:14-07:00","id":1140917,"title":"","content":"I'd like to make a request. I'm having difficulty making a child ghost to use as the main antagonist in an adventure I'm writing. The child haunts the orphanage he died in, collecting other ghosts so he can have &quot;friends&quot; to play with. He even torments and kills living people to add to his collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13542-shadowdragon","name":"Shadowdragon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-16T22:29:17-07:00","id":1140987,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: The Child Ghost</b><br /> <br /> Rules as Written, a standard Ghost caps out at Rank power , and this fellow is going to need to be Rank 3 in order to serve the role you need. To do this with the least amount of house-rule, I would suggest that the Orphanage itself carries much of the spirits power. Having an Underworld Gate in the basement that opens on a semi regular basis would allow the Ghost to gather power in the Underworld, and then return o Twilight to collect more friends. The protagonists then have the two-fold issue of defeating the ghost and closing the gate so he cannot return. <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>The Orphan</b></span><br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 8, Finesse 6, Resistance 6, Willpower 10, Essence 20<br /> <b>Initiative:</b> 12<br /> <b>Defense:</b> 6<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 18<br /> <b>Size:</b> 4<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 10<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Playful, <b>Vice</b> Selfish<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> To find New Friends<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Anchor [Orphanage] 3<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Must Find a New Friend once a Month<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Consecrated Salt; Favorite Toy<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Image, Materialize, Possess, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina: </b>Dement,Hallucination, Host Jump, Maze (as the Dread Power), Mortal Mask, Sign, Telekinesis</span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:20:37-07:00","id":1148350,"title":"","content":"Have you made an update for the necroamalgam from Boston Unveiled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T10:56:06-07:00","id":1148365,"title":"","content":"Is that a ghost or something of that ilk?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T11:02:21-07:00","id":1148368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1148350#post1148350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you made an update for the necroamalgam from Boston Unveiled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of a golem ghost:<br /> ]<span style=\"font-family:LinotypeZapfino\">Necroamalgams </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Wise adherents of the Moros Watchtower warn of </span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\"><i>necroamalgams </i></span><span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">that spawn in the crush of unhallowed bodies in a communal grave. These monsters may have half a dozen heads and arms that sprout from a twisted collection of bones and withered organs. Denied identity in death, the necroamalgams seek revenge on the living. They cow mages with bellowing cries or (especially in the case of amalgams of children) an eerie, singsong chorus. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Rumor has it that a mage can destroy a necroamalgam by confronting it with the names of its component ghosts \u2014 although she must first discover those names. The portion or body part associated with each name supposedly turns to dust upon hearing its name, weakening the remaining whole. If all of its names (anywhere from three to 10, depending on its size) are spoken, the creature is totally destroyed. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Although the necroamalgams are a small minority in Copp\u2019s Hill Burial Ground, they are common enough to represent a serious hazard to the unprepared. These beings actually exist around the world in mass, unhallowed graves. It\u2019s rumored that dark Moros (such as the Tremere) nurture necroamalgams by engineering the creation of such graves. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Goudy\">Statistics for a five-ghost necroamalgam follow. Rules for larger or smaller versions appear in parenthesis. </span><span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">Attributes: Power 7 (2 + 1 per component ghost), </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">Finesse 2, Resistance 3<br /> Willpower: 3<br /> Max Essence: 10 (2 per component ghost)<br /> Morality: 3<br /> Virtue: Fortitude<br /> Vice: Envy<br /> Defense: 7 (equal to Power; necroamalgams always </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">have a higher Power than Finesse)<br /> Initiative: 5<br /> Speed: 19 (Power + Finesse + 10)<br /> Size: 10 (5 +1 per component ghost)<br /> Corpus: 13 (Resistance + Size)<br /> Special: Two physical actions/turn. (Necroamalgams </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:DeadHistoryRoman\">can take one additional instant physical action per turn for every three of its component ghosts, rounded up. </span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12662-bestial-warlust","name":"bestial Warlust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-09T11:27:22-07:00","id":1148381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1148368#post1148368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Necroamalgams</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i0.kym-cdn.com/photos/images/original/000/582/621/da3.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T06:25:50-07:00","id":1149067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>bestial Warlust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie?p=1148350#post1148350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you made an update for the necroamalgam from Boston Unveiled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Try this! <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Necroamalgam</b></span><br /> A rare type of Ghost, the Necroamalgam is a bizarre composite of multiple entities merged into a single being. They most frequently arise from unmarked mass graves that lay near an open Avernian Gate. They speak in a chorus of shrieking voices. The entities are typically comprised of between three to a dozen ghosts, and manifest as a twisted mass of bones, skulls, and withered flesh, the more entities that comprise its form, the greater its power.<br /> The circumstances of their burial have denied the individual ghosts that make up the Necroamalgam their identities, which leaves the gestalt with little but jealousy and contempt for the living.<br /> The example below is for a Necroamalgam comprised of roughly 3-6 entities.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank</b> 2[Ghost]<br /> Power 7 Finesse 2, Resistance 5, Willpower 7, Essence 15<br /> <b>Corpus</b> 15, <b>Size</b> 10, <b>Initiative</b> 7, <b>Defense</b> 5, <b>Speed</b> 19<br /> <b>Virtue</b> Coordinated, <b>Vice</b> Enraged<br /> <b>Aspiration:</b> to lash out at the living, to be remembered<br /> <b>Influence:</b> Anchor (Mass Grave) 2, Jealousy 1<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Being confronted with the name of one of its component ghosts weakens it, speaking all the names destroys it<br /> <b>Bane:</b> A grave marker dedicated to one of its component ghosts<br /> <b>Manifestation:</b> Avernian Gateway, Image, Materialize, Twilight Form<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Awe, Banshee Wail*, Phantom Arsenal*, Regenerate, Stalwart<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Numina \u2013 Banshee Wail: </b>The entity creates an earsplitting scream that deafens anyone nearby. Anyone within 20 yards of the entity must succeed on a Resolve + Stamina roll \u2013 the number of successes gained or suffer the Stunned and Deafened Tilt. The Numen costs one Essence to activate.<br /> <br /> <b>Numina \u2013 Phantom Arsenal: </b>The entity spends 1 Essence point to manifest blades, claws, fangs, hooks or other appropriate weaponry. The modification acts as a +1L weapon. By spending an additional point of essence, this weapon gains the \u201c9-Again\u201d quality.</span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T07:00:28-07:00","id":1149080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></